(#$comment #$AnalogyMatch "An #$AnalogyMatch is the result of a #$matchBetween two #$AnalogyCases.  The Base description is the historical precedent or case, the target is the current situation.  The result of the comparison is a set of mappings (#$AnalogyMappings).  The comparison itself is reified because there are aspects of the comparison that are shared across multiple mappings, and it is potentially useful to talk about the existence (or lack thereof) of mappings satisfying particular properties with respect to a comparison.  For example, consider comparing Operation Desert Storm to WW2.  There are several different ways to view this comparison, each corresponding to a different mapping.  Note, #$AnalogyMatch is very much like #$AnalogyCorrespondence but the first links cases and the second links items, or statements, in cases.") 
