(#$comment #$commonMotiveFor "(#$commonMotiveFor GOAL AGT ACT-TYPE ROLE) means that AGT's playing ROLE in ACT-TYPE is often motivated by AGT's possessing GOAL. Note the 'direction' of the frequency relationship here. (#$commonMotiveFor GOAL AGT ACT-TYPE ROLE) means that, in some reasonably high percentage of cases in which AGT plays ROLE in ACT-TYPE, she is motivated by GOAL.  It does not mean that, in some reasonably high percentage of cases in which AGT possesses GOAL, she participates in ACT-TYPE.  E.g., a common motive for a company to sponsor a float in a parade is to generate publicity.  It does not follow that
companies commonly seek to achieve their goal of generating publicity by sponsoring floats in parades. Obviously, 'commonly' and 'frequently' are rather vague statistical notions.  The intent here is just to parallel their use in ordinary reasoning.") 
