(#$comment #$interResultArgReln "(#$interResultArgReln FUNC N RELN) means that a NAT using FUNC (in the former's arg0 position) denotes something RESULT that stands in the #$BinaryPredicate RELN to the thing ARGN appearing in FUNC's Nth argument position within the NAT, with RESULT appearing as the first argument of
RELN and ARGN appearing as the second argument of RELN.  That is, if 
(FUNC ARG1...ARGN...) = RESULT, then (RELN RESULT ARGN) is true.  For example,
(#$interResultArgReln #$SubPathInsideRegionFn 2 #$pathInsideRegion) means that the result of applying #$SubPathInsideRegionFn to a given PATH and REGION is a 
#$pathInsideRegion of REGION. See also #$interArgResultReln.") 
