(#$comment #$RelativeAttribute "This is the collection of instances of the collection
#$AttributeValue that can be used to describe things in their relationship
relatively or  with respect to some other thing. These values are typically
underdetermined or vague outside a specified context. Practically, ternary
relations that are specializations of #$hasAttributeWithRespectTo are
likely to be used to  reflect the relativity of such attributions. Example,
Pathogenic. (#$hasAttributeWithRespectTo #$Anthrax-Bacterium  #$Pathogenic
#$Person) means that B. anthracis is a human pathogen. #$Difficult is a
borderline example. For instance, we might say that (hasAttributes
SpeakingEnglish Difficult) which means that speaking is inherently
difficult.   However, others might claim that this would make little sense
unless relativized to a potential speaker, i.e., speaking english is not
inherently difficult but may be difficult for some speakers.") 
