(#$comment #$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn "#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn is a Cyc function, in particular, an element of #$IndividualDenotingFunction. It is one of several functions used to denote so-called generic values for a wide variety of attributes. When ATT is a type of attribute, (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn ATT) returns an instance of ATT which is considered `a medium to very high amount of' ATT in the current context. Clearly enough, more could be said about such an instance; in particular, either that it is a medium amount of ATT, or that it is a high amount of ATT, or that it is a very high amount of ATT. #$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn should only be used when there is not enough information available to the cyclist to make one of these stronger assertions.") 
