(#$comment #$directedCycleInSystem "(#$directedCycleInSystem CYCLE SYS) means that CYCLE is a cycle in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS that observes the directions of paths in SYS, i.e., all parts of CYCLE that are paths in SYS must observe the orders or directions of the paths in SYS.  For example, if PATH is a path in SYS directed from X to Y in SYS, and if LINK is a link in SYS directed from Y to X, and in addition if LINK is different from PATH, then (#$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn (#$TheList X PATH Y LINK X)) is a cycle in SYS that observes the directions of paths in SYS. Note that in a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, every loop in SYS is a directed cycle in SYS.  Otherwise a directed cycle is a 'proper' cycle, i.e., it is the concatenation of some directed paths in SYS.") 
