(#$bugtraqDiscussionText #$Bugtraq925 "Winamp, a program for playing mp3 and other audio files, uses  playlist files (*.pls) to store lists of   files for playback. The code that reads these files has an unchecked  buffer which can be   overflowed to cause arbitrary code to be executed. If an entry longer  than 580 bytes is specified in   the file, EIP gets overwritten.   This vulnerability can only be exploited remotely by convincing  someone to download the hostile   playlist and load it into Winamp. IE5 will download .pls files  without user confirmation if winamp is   installed.") 
