(#$comment #$feelsTowardsPersonType "(#$feelsTowardsPersonType AGENT PERSONTYPE
  FEELINGTYPE ATTRIBUTE) says that AGENT
  has FEELINGTYPE to the ATTRIBUTE'th degree
  towards PERSONTYPE.  This predicate is useful
  in conveying notions of #$Prejudice and 
   preference -- notions for which 
   #$feelsTowardsObject are not especially 
    well-suited; having feelings towards a 
group is by no means identical to having 
feelings towards each member of that group.
  Examples of how to use this predicate: To say that
   the KKK feels a great deal of hostility towards
  people of African descent, one can say
 '(#$feelsTowardsPersonType #$KuKluxKlan
   #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks
   #$Hostility #$MediumToVeryHigh).'  To say
  that each individual Klansmen is so hostile, we can use
  the rule, '(#$implies (#$hasMembers 
   #$KuKluxKlan ?HICK) (#$feelsTowardsPersonType
 ?HICK #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks
 #$Hostility #$MediumToVeryHigh)).'  See the
  #$salientAssertions to get a sense of how
  feelings towards a group relate to the 
   individual members of that group.") 
