(#$comment #$quantityInfluenceFunction "(#$quantityInfluenceFunction TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive time slices of THING is subjected to some influence.  If that influence were to be expressed, e.g. in the absence of other influences, then the shape of that function would be one characteristic of elements of FUNCTION-TYPE.  Unlike #$quantityChangeFunction, #$quantityInfluenceFunction does not necessarily entail a change in the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for THING.  It can be used to directly infer #$quantityChangeFunction in the absence of other influences.  If other influences are present, the relative strengths of each influence along with the direction of each influence can be summed to infer a final #$quantityChangeFunction.  See also #$quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength.") 
