(#$comment #$conveyor-Stationary "(#$conveyor-Stationary TRAN CONV) means that in the transportation event TRAN, CONV is a conveyor just like a #$transporter except it does not move together with the #$transportees along the path of the transportation.  For example, a #$River can move a boat [#$Watercraft] from one location to another, and a #$ConveyorBelt can move some objects from one place to another, without itself moving translationally, i.e., the river does not change its location (although some pieces of #$Water in the river do) together with the boat, nor does the #$ConveyorBelt move with the objects on it from place to place (though some parts of it do).") 
