(#$comment #$EvacuatingAPlace "A collection of actions.  In each instance of #$EvacuatingAPlace, some person, animal, or organization leaves the place it had been 'occupying' (e.g., a house, office, geographical region) in response to some perceived danger.  In English, 'evacuating' is used mostly to denote flight prompted by a systematic threat to agents of a certain type or in a certain place. In this sense, leaving your home in response to an approaching hurricane or enemy army counts as 'evacuating,' while leaving your home to avoid an angry rival may not.  The Cyc collection #$EvacuatingAPlace includes both cases.  Note that the performer of an  #$EvacuatingAPlace may be evacuating herself or another agent or both.  If an intelligent agent is evacuating herself from a place, she is both the #$primaryObjectMoving in and the performer of that action.  If an intelligent agent is evacuating another agent(s) from a place (the latter agents need not be intelligent), those being moved are the #$primaryObjectMovings, while those doing the moving are the performers and may or may not also be #$primaryObjectMovings.") 
