(#$comment #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegion "The collection of all instances of #$CountrySubsidiary that
are administered by some #$subOrganizations of a country's military
for purposes of military organization and control.  Generally, but not
always, a #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegion will be a
#$geographicalSubRegions of the country whose military administers it.
The borders of a country's #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegions may or may
not parallel the borders of such provinces and subsidiaries as may be
administered by civilian governmental authority: there is, in most
cases, a correlation between this congruence of borders and the extent
to which military and civil authorities are intermingled within the
country.") 
