(#$comment #$genNatTerm-ArgLast "This predicate is used to deduce lexical assertions, including
#$multiWordStrings, about non-atomic terms (NATs) where the functions
act as linguistic modifiers of their arguments.  (#$genNatTerm-ArgLast
FUNC STRINGS CONSTRAINT) means that, for NATs created using the unary
#$ReifiableFunction FUNC with the argument ARG, one can deduce new
lexical assertions about the term (FUNC ARG) based on the lexical
assertions for ARG, using STRINGS as a modifier.  For instance,
from (#$genNatTerm-ArgLast #$LeftFn (\"left\") #$Noun) and (#$denotation
#$Foot-TheWord #$SimpleNoun 1 #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart), one can deduce
(#$multiWordString (\"left\") #$Foot-TheWord #$SimpleNoun (#$LeftFn
#$Foot-AnimalBodyPart)).  This allows the phrases \"left foot\" and \"left feet\" to be
both generated and understood.  CONSTRAINT must be an instance of
#$TermPhrasesConstraint.  See also #$genNatTerm-multiWordString,
#$genNatTerm-compoundString, and #$termPhrases.") 
