(#$cyclistNotes #$MissionStatement-Organization "This constant, together with #$missionOfOrganization, provides            a way of stating the purposes or missions of            an organization in #$CycL just as #$statementOfPurpose            provides a way of stating the purpose of an organization in            English.  The definition of this collection assumes the mission            statement of an organization is an #$Agreement in which the            #$agreeingAgents are members of the #$Organization.  To            state different parts of the mission statement for an            organization using this collection one can use #$ist,            #$ist-Agreement, or simply assert the appropriate            #$CycFormula in the appropriate #$Microtheory that is an            instance of #$MissionStatement-Organization.  It is probably            best to use #$ist-Agreement, but at the moment this constant            is not well-supported by the inference engine.  To get             queries to work, one may have to use the third option above,            though in other respects, it is the least preferable.            Meyer, July 21, 1999.") 
