(#$comment #$testNthPrimingAsk "(#$testNthPrimingAsk TQM N PAM) means that before the ask test (#$TestQuestionMicrotheory) TQM is run, the testing facility will run PAM.  N indicates the order in which to call priming asks.  The testing facility assumes that if there are any priming asks to be done that the first one to be run has N equal 1. The following priming ask is assumed to be the nth plus 1.  If there is no nth plus 1 test, then the testing facility ceases running priming asks and moves to ask the main ask, i.e. TQM.  Note that PAM should be a #$genlMt of TQM in order that results cached in that microtheory are visible in TQM.  Also, all assertions in the TQM need to be visible to each of its PAMs.  Thus a pair of foward rules exists in order to ensure that the correct #$genlMt assertions get added.") 
