(#$comment #$signatories "The predicate #$signatories relates a particular agreement to the
  agents who have signed the agreement.  (#$signatories AGR PARTY) does not
  entail (#$agreeingAgents AGR PARTY), as in some cases an agreement does not
  enter into force directly upon its being signed, but only after some
  other action has occurred.  For example, the following is true of certain
  international agreements: although a given country's leader or other
  representative has signed the agreement on behalf of her country--
  thus making the country a signatory--the country cannot be considered an
  agreeing agent unless and until the country's government as a whole has
  ratified the agreement.  Nor, of course, does entailment hold in the
  opposite direction, due to the existence of verbal agreements.  Depending
  on the nature of the agreement, a signatory might be a person who has
  physically put his signature on a copy of the agreement, or (as in the
  above example) might be a country or other instance of #$MultiIndividualAgent
  for whom the actual signer is acting as representative.") 
