(#$comment #$CoalitionInformationDesignation "A subcollection of #$InformationDesignation.  Instances of this
collection are attributes of information.  Specifically, they are designations or classifications
of information created by coalitions between governments.  For instance, if the US formed a coalition with
Israel for operations in the middle east, they might designate the information accessible by only those members of 
the coalition. The designations in this scheme would be instances of #$CoalitionInformationDesignation.  The scheme might borrow
from the US governments preexisting method of classifying information, but could include novel names to prevent confusion
or misapplication of the scope of information accessible by the coalition members:  for instance, 'US-IsraelSecret' might 
replace the usual 'Secret' classification used by the US government because it refers to distinct information sources,
but it could still preserve the meaning of the term 'secret' as understood by the US government.") 
