(#$comment #$infoTransferred-Implicitly "(infoTransferred-Implicitly ITE INFO) means that ?INFO is part of the implicit information content of the InformationTransferEvent ?ITE. What is meant by  'implicit' here? Consider the following: the class of  #$InformationTransferEvents is quite large, and includes things like grunting in order to express disgust, and also stating 'I'm disgusted.' The proposition communicated by the English sentence 'I am disgusted' would be part of the explicit information content of the sentence, but not of the grunt, which conveys it implicitly. Another way of approaching this is to consider the difference between the denotation  of what is expressed in ITEs, and what may be easily inferred from them in context. For example, if I say in a sarcastic voice, 'Gee, that hat looks just great,' I may be communicating 'What an ugly hat,' but that would not be part of the explicit information of my utterance. See also #$infoTransferred-Explicitly.") 
