(#$comment #$DestructivePotential "#$DestructivePotential is a collection of attributes representing
scalar indices of the destructive potential of an #$Event or a
#$SomethingExisting.  The thing whose destructive potential is being
gauged may be a particular weather event, like a tornado or a
hurricane, or a situation, like an international arms build-up.  It
may be also be a weapon.  In any case, #$DestructivePotential is
measured primarily by looking at the #$DegreeOfDamage caused by a
typical instance or typical use of the thing whose
#$DestructivePotential is being gauged.") 
(#$comment #$GenerationCulture "A specialization of #$AgeCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture defined at least in part by the fact 
  that its core participants were born or came of age during a 
  certain (roughly ten- to twenty-year) period.  Interesting 
  instances of #$GenerationCulture are often defined in relation 
  to some significant social or historical event; for example, 
  the Baby Boomers are defined as having been born in the US in 
  the years immediately following the end of WWII.") 
