(#$comment #$formsBorderPart "This predicate is used to assert that a particular #$SpatialThing-Localized is part of the conventional abstraction that is a #$GeopoliticalBorder. (#$formsBorderPart PART WHOLE) means that all of the points along the border-part PART are also points along the border WHOLE.
We would use this predicate, eg, to say that the border between Texas and Mexico forms part of the border of the United States:  (#$formsBorderPart (#$BorderBetweenFn #$Texas-State #$Mexico) (#$BorderFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)).") 
