(#$cyclistNotes #$InternationalWaters "Since territorial waters can become
#$InternationalWaters and cease to be #$InternationalWaters, the fact
that a particular territorial claim is an #$InternationalWaters should
never be asserted 'simpliciter', but ought always to be wrapped in an
assertion using #$holdsIn, so that the appropriate subAbstractions is
specified.  Ordinarily, territorial seas, exclusive economic zones,
contiguous zones, and maritime claims are open to international
traffic and trade, and therefore are considered InternationalWaters,
even though the international community accepts them as being under
the control of specific nations.") 
