(#$comment #$cfImplies "The predicate #$cfImplies is used to represent
counterfactual implication. (#$cfImplies A B) means that if A had been
the case (true), then B would be the case (true).  In the current
representation, (#$cfImplies A B) entails (#$not A), in the actual
context.  That constraint is among #$salientAssertions on #$cfImplies.
(In a broader treatment of counterfactuals, that requirement could be
dropped.)  #$cfImplies is used to reason about the differences from the actual context (i.e., the
B's) that would occur if A were true.") 
