(#$comment #$SubPathInsideRegionFn "This function takes a spatial path together with a spatial region it intersects (see #$pathIntersectsRegion) and returns
the longest continuous segment of the path that is inside the 
region.  More precisely, (#$SubPathInsideRegionFn PATH REGION) 
denotes the single longest #$subPaths of PATH (if any) that is 
#$pathInsideRegion REGION.  If PATH does not intersect REGION,
then #$SubPathInsideRegionFn is #$undefined for these arguments.
If PATH weaves in and out of REGION more than once, this 
function returns only the longest continous subpath of PATH
that is inside of REGION (should there be no unique longest
such segment, again PATH is undefined for these arguments).") 
