(#$comment #$givesSupportToAgentForGoal "This predicate can be used to indicate when one agent aids another
agent in reaching some goal.  (#$givesSupportToAgentForGoal
AGENT1 AGENT2 GOAL) means two things: (i) the instance 
AGENT2 of #$Agent has the goal GOAL, i.e. 
(#$goals AGENT2 GOAL) and (ii) the instance AGENT1 
of #$Agent provides some sort of support to AGENT2
in AGENT2's attempt to obtain GOAL.  Note that AGENT2
need not actually obtain GOAL for GAFS using this predicate
to hold.") 
