(#$comment #$accessibleFrom "This predicate relates pairs of nearby regions or
objects that are so situated that an unaided human could 
move directly to the second from the first.  
(#$accessibleFrom HERE THERE) means that HERE and THERE 
are places -- i.e. either regions or objects (like rooms
and rooftops) that are capable of containing or supporting
a human -- such that the average human could, more or less 
directly, get from being in/on HERE to being in/on THERE
without excessive difficulty or risk, and without the use 
of special equipment.  For example, one room is accessible 
from another if the door between them is unlocked, but not if
the door is locked.  This predicate is not symmetric as, for 
example, it might be possible to jump from one rooftop to a 
lower rooftop yet not possible to climb back.") 
