(#$comment #$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable "The predicate #$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable is used to
describe the ways in which types of existing things can function and
are intended by their designers to
function. (#$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable OBJTYPE SITTYPE ROLE) means
that instances of OBJTYPE are intended by OBJTYPE's designer to play
role ROLE in situations or events of type SITTYPE, and that instances
of OBJTYPE can play role ROLE in situations or events of type SITTYPE.
For example, instances of #$Clothing-Generic are intended to be
capable of being removed and being put on. We can represent this by
(#$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable #$Clothing-Generic #$Undressing
#$objectRemoved), and
(#$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable #$Clothing-Generic
#$PuttingOnAClothingItem #$objectActedOn) See also
#$typeBehaviorCapable and #$typePrimaryFunction.") 
