(#$comment #$unitMultiplicationFactor "(#$unitMultiplicationFactor
SMALL-UNITS BIG-UNITS NUM) means that there are NUM SMALL-UNITS in
every BIG-UNITS.  In other words, to convert from a measure in
BIG-UNITS to a measure in SMALL-UNITS multiply by NUM.  For example,
(#$unitMultiplicationFactor #$Inch #$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 12) means that
one multiplies feet by twelve when converting from feet to inches.  NUM must be greater than or equal to 1.  SMALL-UNITS and BIG-UNITS must be
elements of the same #$InterconvertibleUnitType.  See also #$QuantityConversionFn.") 
