(#$comment #$transferRelay-Generic "This predicate can be used to indicate whatever acts as a relay in instances of           #$GeneralizedTransfer and plays as well a primarily passive though crucial role.            (for a predicate to indicate instances of #$Thing playing            an active role see #$transferRouter-Generic).            (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS THING) means that THING acts as a relay            in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANS but primarily in a passive capacity.            For example, suppose a trip TRANS via             airplane taking a person PER from New York to Austin makes a stop in #$CityOfOmahaNB,            where PER changes flights.  If 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport' is the instance of             #$Airport-Physical located in the #$CityOfOmahaNB, then we can say that            'CityOfOmahaNBAirport' is a relay point or node in the #$GeneralizedTransfer            TRANS of PER and represent            this by (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport').") 
