(#$comment #$mtsConditionallyConflict "(#$mtsConditionallyConflict ANT PROP MTPROVE MTNOT) means that a
conditional of the form (implies ANT PROP) is provable in MTPROVE
while a conditional of the form (implies ANT (not PROP)) is provable
in MTNOT.  Equivalently, it means that if ANT is asserted in a context to which both MTPROVE and MTNOT
have access, it will be the case that (#$mtsConflict PROP MTPROVE MTNOT).
Trivially, (#$mtsConflict PROP MTPROVE MTNOT) implies
(#$mtsConditionallyConflict ANT PROP MTPROVE MTNOT) for any #$CycFormula instance ANT.") 
