(#$cyclistNotes #$repliesTo-CoABSCommunicating "Because the assumptions governing instances of
#$SoftwareAgentConversation in the CoABS 'Grid' domain are fairly
constrained, we are somewhat safer in giving sufficient conditions for
the relation (#$answersCoABSCommunicating ACT REPLY) to hold.
Specifically, if COMM is a #$SoftwareAgentConversation, and ACT and
REPLY are #$subEvents of COMM such that REPLY #$followsInProgression after
ACT in COMM, and the peformers of ACT and REPLY are different and the       
#$communicationTarget of REPLY is the performer of ACT and the
#$recipientOfInfo of ACT is the performer of REPLY, then
(#$repliesTo-CoABSCommunicating ACT REPLY).  An 'answers' relation that
satisfies weaker conditions could of course still hold: thus, e.g.,
one speech act could still be in answer to another even if the
relation between them was not #$followsInProgression.  See the definitional
constraints on the predicate, however.") 
