(#$comment #$RootPrivilege "An attribute of a #$ComputerProgramCopy running on a
#$CompuationalSystem with a #$Unix operating system. A program has
#$RootPrivilege if it is able to modify, create, or delete those
files on the system that it is configured to access.  
For example, yppasswd will have #$RootPriviledge on the instance of 
#$PasswordFile in a #$Unix system. #$RootPrivilege allows a normal user User001 (i.e., (not
(#$hasRootAccount User001 RootAccount001)), to execute a program that
requires root access, . However, these types of programs
constitute an #$SUIDRootVulnerability.") 
