(#$comment #$typePrimaryFunction "The predicate #$typePrimaryFunction can be used to represent the           primary use associated with some type of object (usually instances           of #$PhysicalDevice but also instances of #$Organization, or anything           else that can be said to have a function).             (#$typePrimaryFunction OBJ_TYPE SIT_TYPE ROLE) means that            instances of OBJ_TYPE are primarily intended to participate            in situations of type SIT_TYPE in the instance of #$Role ROLE.  For example,           the primary use associated with any instance of #$ElectricalToaster is           making toast: we can represent this by           (#$typePrimaryFunction #$ElectricalToaster #$MakingToast #$deviceUsed).           Aa another example, the primary use associated with a government intelligence           organization is performing instances of #$IntelligenceProcess.           We can represent this as           (#$typePrimaryFunction #$GovernmentIntelligenceOrganization             #$IntelligenceProcess #$performedBy).  See also           #$typeBehaviorCapable, #$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable and #$primaryFunction.") 
