(#$comment #$Series "The collection of situations in which 2 or more ''parts'' or ''members'' are ordered in some linear fashion, by some relations among them.  For example, the line of people at a ticket booth, an alphabetized set of words, or the series of pitches in a baseball game.  In every instance of #$Series, there is some relation by which its members are ordered (see #$seriesOrderedBy); this is in contrast to an instance of #$List, in which the only ordering relation on its members is that of succession in the list.") 
