(#$cyclistNotes #$authorizesAgentToDo "As a default, it seems reasonable to assume that when an agent is given authorization to do something, there is a unique agent that gives the authorization. Therefore, in an assertion of the form (#$authorizesAgentToDo GRANTING AGENT ACTION-TYPE), although there is no explicit mention of the granter of permission, that agent is referred to indirectly through the reference to GRANTING. (This is why #$authorizesAgentToDo is ternary rather than quaternary.) If you use #$authorizesAgentToDo and you want to make reference to the giver of permission, add a clause of the form (#$performedBy GRANTING PERMITTER), where 'PERMITTER' refers to the granter of permission.") 
