(#$comment #$rationalIntermediateGoals "(#$rationalIntermediateGoals AGT 
CYCFORMULA1 CYCFORMULA2)
means that, 
given the agent's overall beliefs and goals, it would be rational for the
agent to adopt CYCFORMULA1 as an #$intermediateGoals
in order to achieve CYCFORMULA2.
Note that the sense of 'rationality' used here
is merely 'economic' rationality; i.e., rationality
relative to attaining ones goals, given one's beliefs. No
evaluation of the rationality of the ends, or of the beliefs
of the agent, is presumed here. Note also that, as a default,
Cyc assumes that agents act rationally, i.e., that they adopt
as #$intermediateGoals their #$rationalIntermediateGoals.") 
