(#$comment #$iteIllocutionaryForce "The predicate #$iteIllocutionaryForce is used to indicate the illocutionary force that a communication act has as an attribute. So (#$iteIllocutionaryForce COM ILLFORCE) states that COM has the illocutionary force IllFORCE associated with it.  The presence of such an attribute allows us to distinguish communication acts whose propositional content may be the same.  For instance, the information conveyed in an act whose illocutionary force is #$Predict may differ from the information conveyed in an act whose illocutionary force is #$Order even if the propositional content of both acts is the same.  See also #$componentIF.") 
