(#$comment #$FunctionTheMathematicalType "#$FunctionTheMathematicalType is the collection of functions.  Each instance of #$FunctionTheMathematicalType represents a mapping from one set of objects (its domain) to another set of objects (its range).  Given an object in the domain, the function maps to only one object in the range.  This class includes elements of #$Function-Denotational, the collection of terms which are used syntactically as function in CycL.  It also includes abstract functions, such as elements of #$Distribution, and the (non-denumerably many) one-to-one correspondences that must exist between the positive integers and the rational numbers. ") 
