(#$comment #$EdgeOnObject "The collection of all edges on objects.
For a two-dimensional object, its boundaries other the edges that
define the object.  Edges intersect at corners.  For a three
dimensional object the edges are the boundaries of the surfaces that
are the outer surfaces of the object (see #$objectSurfaces).
Some objects, like spheres, hairs, poles and typical burrs, have no
edges. A discus has one, round, edge; a typical sheet has four edges.  
A mountain ridge might have only a single edge.  A solid polyhedron 
has six or more edges.") 
