(#$comment #$commutativeInArgs "(#$commutativeInArgs REL ARGNUM-1 ARGNUM-2 ... ARGNUM-N) means that REL is commutative with respect to each of the argument positions ARGNUM-1, ARGNUM-2, ..., and ARGNUM-N.  For example,
(#$commutativeInArgs REL 1 2) means that the first and second
arguments to REL are commutative, but not necessarily the third
or greater argument positions.  (#$commutativeInArgs REL 2 3 5)
means that the second, third, and fifth argument positions of REL
are commutative, but not necessarily the first, fourth, or any positions
greater than the fifth.
(Since REL is an instance of #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation, it 
must have at least two argument positions that are commutative, and at least
one that is _not_ commutative.)") 
