(#$comment #$Monitoring "The subcollection of #$Events in which an instance (or more) of #$Agent           monitors, i.e. keeps track of, some situation, generally a fairly large-scale,           ongoing situation, such as the movement of a storm, a military operation, or           a series of related crimes.  Every instance of #$Monitoring should have two           #$subEventTypes: the first the establishment of communication links with           relevant information sources and the second instances of #$InformationGathering           from these sources.  These two types can occur any number of times, although           the first instance of the latter type must always be preceded by an instance           of the former.  For instance, in monitoring the movement of a storm, some           instance of #$Agent may establish some communication link with a            weather station acquiring information about the storm and then gather information           about the storm from the station.  This could be repeated with different           weather stations in the same instance of #$Monitoring as long as the information           gathered concerns the same storm.  There are no restrictions on the nature of           the communication links or the information sources... [More].") 
