(#$cyclistNotes #$evidentialSupport "It is important to bear in mind that #$evidentialSupport involves a notion of *reasonableness* of degree of belief. Since it is not reasonable to believe that a proposition and its negation are both true, it should never be true that (#$holdsIn TIME (#$and (#$evidentialSupport AGENT PROP-A #$High) (#$evidentialSupport AGENT PROP-B #$High))), when PROP-A and PROP-B are incompatible propositions.") 
