(#$cyclistNotes #$transferRelay-Generic "Note that whether an instance of #$Thing counts as a #$transferRelay-Generic                is completely relative to an instance of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  For instance,                suppose an airline flight TRANS_TO_OMAHA leaves Austin and arrives in the                #$CityOfOmahaNB and many passengers consider this their final destination,                but at least one person does not and leaves on a different flight to                New York within an hour of arriving in Omaha.  Let this instance of                #$GeneralizedTransfer be TRANS_TO_NY.  In this example, we could assert                (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS_TO_NY 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport') where                'CityOfOmahaNBAirport' is the instance of #$Airport-Physical located                in the #$CityOfOmahaNB, but it would be                 incorrect to assert (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS_TO_OMAHA 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport').                What would be correct is (#$toLocation TRANS_TO_OMAHA 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport').") 
