(#$comment #$FalsePositives "(#$testStatus-Automatic TEST RUN #$FalsePositives) means that at the time RUN happened, the test specified by TEST functioned such that at least one of the results obtained was not specified as a target bindings (see #$testAnswersCycL).  Such returned bindings are either correct answers and the relevant target bindings have not yet been specified or they are incorrect, 'false positive' returns.  Thus, (#$testStatus-Automatic TEST RUN #$FalsePositives),  is incompatible with (#$testStatus-Automatic TEST RUN #$Hit-Exact).  By contrast, #$FalsePositives is compatible with #$Hit-InExact  but neither one of these two entails the other.  Likewise, #$FalsePositives is compatible with #$MissedSome but neither one of these two entails the other.") 
