(#$comment #$genNatTerm-multiWordString "This predicate is used to deduce #$multiWordString assertions about
non-atomic terms (NATs).  (#$genNatTerm-multiWordString FUNC STRINGS
WORD POS CONSTRAINT) means that, for NATs created using the unary
#$ReifiableFunction FUNC, one can deduce (#$multiWordString
NEW-STRINGS WORD POS (FUNC ARG)), where NEW-STRINGS combines STRINGS
plus the phrases for ARG that meet CONSTRAINT.  For instance,
(#$genNatTerm-multiWordString #$PlayerOfInstrumentFn NIL
#$Play-TheWord #$AgentiveNoun #$singular) gives rise to deductions
like (#$multiWordString (\"piano\") #$Play-TheWord #$AgentiveNoun
(#$PlayerOfInstrumentFn #$Piano-Acoustic)).  This allows the phrases
\"piano player\" and \"piano players\" to be both generated and understood.
CONSTRAINT must be an instance of #$TermPhrasesConstraint.  See also
#$genNatTerm-compoundString, #$genNatTerm-ArgLast, and #$termPhrases.") 
