(#$comment #$enables-StaticConduciveFactor "This predicate represents the idea that an agent may be enabled
to do something not by the occurrence of an event, but simply by finding
herself, more or less statically, in a certain situation. Example: having
residence in midtown Manhattan enables one to attend performances of the
Metropolitan Opera, in the sense of making it more likely that one would be
capable of attending such a performance than one would be if she lived,
say, in Austin. Therefore, (#$enables-StaticConduciveFactor CIRC SIT AGENT
ACT_TYPE) means that, in the circumstance CIRC, the obtaining of SIT makes
it more likely that AGENT would succeed at an instance of ACT_TYPE were she
to attempt than it would be otherwise -- i.e., if SIT did not obtain.") 
