(#$comment #$hasAccess "(hasAccess PERSON OBJ) means that PERSON has access to the individual OBJ.  This predicate is true of PERSON and OBJ whenever PERSON can access OBJ.  It should be construed broadly enough to include the following senses of access: the access one has to physical objects in one's immediate vicinity or to a place the person may go to, the access to information or files one may gain with a remote computer connection, and the sort of access one has to other people (e.g. access to a telephone operator by picking up the phone).  Having access generally precedes possessing or controlling an object.  Note that PERSON may have access to OBJ even though he is not permitted to; that is, (#$hasAccess PERSON OBJ) may be true even though (#$not (#$groupMembers (#$AccessorFn OBJ) PERSON)).") 
