(#$comment #$Solution "A collection of tangible stuffs; a subset of #$Mixture.  Each instance of #$Solution is a #$Mixture of two or more chemically distinct substances.  #$Solutions are homogeneous, meaning that the composition at any one point in the #$Mixture is the same as that at any other point.  In contrast, a #$Suspension is a #$Mixture in which small discontinuous particles are surrounded by a continuous fluid.  The #$solvent of every #$Solution has the #$stateOfMatter #$LiquidStateOfMatter.  Thus #$Solutions also normally exhibit the properties of a liquid, since #$solvents are #$mainConstituents.   Examples of #$Solutions: seawater, a cup of coffee, a tincture of iodine, some vanilla extract.") 
