(#$comment #$Isolate-MilitaryTask "To isolate is to seal off both physically and psychologically an enemy force from his sources of support, to deny the enemy freedom of movement, and to prevent the enemy unit from having contact with other enemy forces. Physical and psychological isolation are interdependent factors. Once isolated, an enemy unit must not be allowed sanctuary within his present position. It is attacked as often as possible. Usually associated with encirclement operations, isolate as a task can be a part of a deliberate attack to facilitate the breach of an enemy's defensive perimeter. This leads to the resulting piecemeal destruction of the enemy force.") 
