(#$comment #$credibility "(#$credibility INFOTR AGT AMOUNT) means that the #$InformationTransferEvent INFOTR has a credibility, or believability, to the #$Agent AGT, of amount AMOUNT. So, for instance, (#$credibility ReadingUSAToday001 #$Kean #$LowToVeryLow) means that #$Kean finds what she is reading in #$USAToday-TheNewspaper in that particular instance fairly unconvincing, and (#$credibility Threatening101 #$OKeefe #$High) means that #$OKeefe finds that particular #$MakingAThreat quite credible.  Note: to say that some agent is credible, write rules stating that any #$Communicating in which that agent is the #$senderOfInfo has a high credibility for whomever receives it. Similarly, to say that some #$InformationBearingThing is credible, say that any #$InformationTransferEvents in which it is the #$informationOrigin has a high credibility for the #$recipientOfInfo.") 
