(#$comment #$WithdrawingARepresentative "Events in which an organization or 
individual withdraws  (one or more) of its/his/her representatives from
another organization, conference, etc.  Examples:  a country calling home 
its ambassador from another country, a company  ordering its representatives
to leave a conference or a negotiating  session.  Instances of
#$WithdrawingARepresentative frequently involve a #$Translation-LocationChange,
as the ambassador leaves the country, the lawyer leaves the place of
negotiations, etc.  (But sometimes merely having a representative refuse to
show up to a meeting is sufficient.) Such events have the individual or
organization being represented as their #$directingAgent. Unilateral decisions to leave by the representative herself/themselves are not  instances of #$WithdrawingARepresentative.") 
