(#$comment #$decreasesCausally "(#$decreasesCausally
EVENT THING SLOT) means that EVENT causes the value of the predicate
SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument position) to decrease
over some time period after the start of EVENT.  This is defined in
terms of #$decreasesCausallyOverPeriod (see also).  Compared with its
value immediately before EVENT, the value of SLOT applied to THING is
guaranteed to be higher immediately following or some time after
EVENT.  This net decrease need not be monotonic.  See
#$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.") 
