(#$comment #$AgentBasedSystemMalfunction "The most general collection of grid error
events; a subset of #$Malfunction, and a subset of #$SystemCondition.
An instance of #$AgentBasedSystemMalfunction is a dynamic state of impairment.  Having a
grid error is an event: it has temporal aspects, it progresses
dynamically, etc., it is not just `being in some static state of
error.'  Some subsets of #$AgentBasedSystemMalfunction are: #$MessageLost,
#$ResourceBudgetExceeded, #$OrphanedTask.  If an event on the grid
produces a solution which actually worsens the problem meant to be
solved, that event contains an element of #$AgentBasedSystemMalfunction.  Each
#$AgentBasedSystemMalfunction is a state of actual, developed error or impairment,
rather than the event of developing an error.  Also note that each
type of error, such as Asthma, is the set of all `cases' or
`instances' of grid events which have that error.") 
