(#$comment #$arrangementObjectTypes "This predicate relates an arrangement of like
objects to a type of object under which all of its members
fall.  (#$arrangementObjectTypes GROUP OBJTYPE) means that
OBJTYPE is an instance of #$ExistingObjectType that all 
#$groupMembers of GROUP are instances of.  For example, if 
the members of GROUP are the trees in a palm grove, then
OBJTYPE could be #$PalmTree.  OBJTYPE need not be one of the 
maximally specific types under which all of GROUP's members 
fall: the grove can still be described as an arrangement of
#$PalmTrees even if all of the members happen to be instances 
of #$DatePalm.  Each instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects 
should have at least one such corresponding object type.  For 
a more specific predicate see #$arrangementNearestObjectTypes.") 
