(#$comment #$NetworkPort "A instance of #$NetworkPort is an information organization
abstraction.  Packets coming in to a computer contain a port
number, and the operating system on the computer directs the
packet to the program assigned the same port number (see
#$programCopyOnPort).  For instance, 
packets sent to the Sendmail program on a computer contain
information that they are bound for port 25, since this is the port
on which Sendmail listens.") 
(#$comment #$StreetCornerFn "(#$StreetCornerFn XING DIRECTION) denotes the
lot of land (if any) that lies adjacent to, and generally to 
the DIRECTION of, XING.  A given intersection will normally 
have four street corners associated with it, corresponding 
to four directions that are approximately 90 degrees apart 
from each other.  For example, if the two streets that 
intersect at XING run north-south and east-west, respectively, 
then there will be street corners to the #$NorthEast-Generally, 
#$NorthWest-Generally, #$SouthEast-Generally, and 
#$SouthWest-Generally of XING.  See also #$atStreetIntersection
and #$directionsOfPath.") 
