(#$comment #$dispersionSource "A binary predicate relating an event in which things are ditributed to the source from which the distribution takes place. For example, in an event of spraying an aerosol from a can, the can is the source of the dispersion: (#$dispersionSource Spraying001 Can001). Similarly, if the explosion of a bomb, Bomb001, causes the distribution-of-shrapnel event, Dist001, then (#$dispersionSource Dist001 Bomb001) is true. Despite the lack of rules to enforce this, not every pair of an instance of PhysicalDistributionEvent and the instance of PartiallyTangible where the distribution intuitively originates will satisfy #$dispersionSource. For example, although Lake Itasca is the headwaters of the Missippi, and therefore in a sense the source of the (very long duration) event in which the Mississippi flows into the Gulf of Mexico, it is not true that (dispersionSource FlowOfTheMississippi Itasca), and not just because there are tributaries of the Mississippi that themselves have source this is not the right kind of distribution event to have a dispersionSource. Finally, note that #$dispersionSource is interesting primarily not for its own sake, but rather for the sake of enabling interesting restrictions to be put on kinds of instances of PhysicalDistributionEvent.") 
