(#$comment #$GroundStamids "An instance of #$GroundStamids is a vehicle-mounted mine detection and marking system for use both on and off road.  It detects metallic and non-metallic mines, through use of multiple sensors, with a standoff capability to prevent mine detonation under the vehicle.  Possible detection sensors are metal detectors and ground penetrating radar.  Teleoperation, or semi-autonomous operation techniques, using the Army Standard Teleoperation System, will be used to provide increased soldier safety.  Mine detection, data processing and display, and mine marking are autonomous.  Mine information is displayed to the system operator, and the operator will disseminate this information through the appropriate channels.  A #$GroundStamids may be used for route clearance missions, leading convoys, detecting the leading edges of minefields, or reconnaissance missions by Engineers, Cavalry, scouts, Military Police, etc. (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)") 
