(#$comment #$suppliers "The predicate suppliers represents a
relationship between two #$Agent-Generics. (#$suppliers AGT1 AGT2)
means that AGT1 supplies some goods or services to AGT2 - usually on
an ongoing basis. When payment is returned for the supplying, one
should use the inverse specialization customers.--Mark Willems,
2/13/98.") 
