(#$comment #$ImposingSanctions "The collection of all impositions of sanctions, each imposition being performed by an #$Agent upon another #$Agent that has some formal relationship to the imposer.  In this #$ScriptType, the main #$Event is an official enactment by the imposer, calculated to lead to events that the recipient is presumed to dislike.  For example, an organization imposes a fine on one of its members, a judge imposes sanctions on an errant lawyer before the court, the Roman Catholic Church excommunicates a miscreant parishioner, or the United Nations declares an oil embargo against a member-state.  The purpose is either to punish the recipient for past disapproved behavior (as in criminal contempt of court, punishing rudeness or dishonesty) or to create an incentive for the recipient to improve future behavior (as in imprisonment for civil contempt of court, designed to force cooperation by a witness).  The imposing #$Agent may or may not have any legitimate legal authority to impose the sanction, and may or may not have any power of enforcing the sanction.  An instance of #$ImposingSanctions is the formal enactment rather than any later acts of enforcement.  This concept is more specific than #$Punishing which includes spanking a baby, pistol-whipping a crime suspect, or retaliation bombing.") 
