(#$comment #$resumeField-ChargeForServices "(resumeField-ChargeForServices ?RESUME ?MONEYRATE) means that the agent charges so much money for its services. The #$MoneyRate includes amount of money per some unit, (usually of time). For example, an agent might charge $10.00 American per hour of work. On the other hand, it might charge by the task. For example, it might charge $1.00 per bit of data it looks up in a table. If the formula for  calculating the charge is more complicated, for example, if resource use is factored in, then this should be specified on the resume. This information is important for  the receiver of payment, the users and for the brokering agents.") 
