(#$comment #$regionalEvent "This predicate can be used to indicate when an instance of #$Event is
'regional.'  (#$regionalEvent EVT SMALLER_REGION LARGER_REGION) means that
(i) both (#$eventOccursAt EVT SMALLER_REGION) and
(#$eventOccursAt EVT LARGER_REGION) hold,
(ii) (#$geographicalSubRegions LARGER_REGION SMALLER_REGION) holds and (iii)
in the context in which this GAF is asserted (represented in part
by LARGER_REGION), EVT is considered a 'regional event.'  For
example, in a context in which LARGER_REGION is #$PlanetEarth, 
a state-wide election in Texas is a 'regional event,' whereas in a
context in which the LARGER_REGION is #$Texas-State, this election
would not be considered 'regional.'") 
