(#$comment #$ResumeFields "The collection of all #$ResumeFields consists in particular fields  on a #$Resume-CoABS. ResumeFields refers to the names of the fields; not to what #$CharacterString is entered in the field. To relate the characterstring with the field name, one can use the predicates of particular fields. For example, one can use the predicate: #$resumeField-GridAddress. The fields are filled out by instances of #$Agent-CoABS. Usually, a resume will be filled out by the agent itself. Only one field has  to be filled out, and this is an address. The fields do not need to be filled out in CycL. It is, however, advantageous to the agent if the fields  are filled out in a language readily understood by other agents, particularly broker and matchmaker agents.") 
