(#$comment #$ElectronicAttack-UDPPacketStorm "#$ElectronicAttack-UDPPacketStorm is a subset of #$ElectronicAttack-DataFloodingComputerCrashing.   It is the collection of instances of UDP packet storming attacks.  In
this kind of attack, the attacker floods the victim's machine with UDP
#$Packet-Internets.  Unlike other versions of UDP packet electronic attacks, such as those involving the use of #$Bonk-MaliciousProgram, the UDP packets may not be corrupt or malformed. Instances of #$ElectronicAttack-UDPPacketStorm are successful when they congest the victim's computer until it cannot handle the incoming data and fails or undergoes an instance of #$ComputerCrashing.") 
