(#$comment #$CycTheCollection "Cyc (like almost all programs) can be thought of as a collection of programs.  There may be many different copies of the program on storage media or in the memory of a computer.  This unit represents that aspect of Cyc.  The unit, #$Cyc has been in the KB for a long time; it has denoted both the general concept of the Cyc program as well as any copy of Cyc running on someone's machine.  The unit #$Cyc gets to stay in the KB, but it now becomes a #$TheTerm and an instance of #$CycTheCollection.  So the things we say about #$Cyc will be true of any other instance of Cyc that is addded to the KB.") 
