(#$comment #$TemporallyIndexicalFirstOrderTerm "An element of #$TemporallyIndexicalFirstOrderTerm is a term the denotation (referent) of which varies over time (or at least might so vary).  In addition, an element of this collection is not a predicate, formula, or function.  However, it may be a non-atomic term, in which case it will not contain free variables.  For example, at any moment during January 1, 1998, the denotation of the constant `#$Tomorrow-Indexical' is January 2, 1998.  [So it's the case that (#$holdsIn (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1998))) (#$equals #$Tomorrow-Indexical (#$DayFn 2 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1998))))).]  But at any moment during January 2, 1998, the denotation of `#$Tomorrow-Indexical' is not January 2, 1998, but January 3, 1998.  As another example, at any moment in 1996, the denotation of `(PresidentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)' is #$BillClinton.  But at any moment in 1990, `(PresidentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)' denotes #$GeorgeBush.") 
