(#$comment #$subAbsBefore "(#$subAbsBefore ?SUPER ?SUB ?TEMP-OB) indicates that ?SUPER and ?SUB are #$SomethingExistings, ?SUB is some #$subAbstrac of ?SUPER, and (#$contiguousAfter ?TEMP-OB ?SUB). This provides one way to talk about pre-conditions for some state-changing process.  For example, 'Egg001 was raw before being scrambled' -- if (#$subAbsBefore Egg001 ?SUB Scrambling001), then ?SUB is raw.  Usually the preferred alternative (because it is simpler) is to use the #$holdsIn representation: (#$holdsIn (#$STIB Scrambling001) 'Egg001 is raw').") 
