(#$comment #$power-Military "(#$power-Military ORG GENERIC-VALUE)
means that the military power of ORG is GENERIC-VALUE.  ORG 
may be any organization which has direct or indirect control over
a military force -- viz.,
a #$Country or an international alliance like #$NATO.
  Military power can be determined in a number of ways: total forces available, total equipment available, 
yearly expenditures, etc. More military power increases the 
chances of success of a #$MilitaryOperation carried out by
ORG. In a given context it might be useful to assert that the
#$UnitedStatesOfAmerica has a lot of military power, and that
#$SaintLucia has very little.") 
