(#$comment #$vehicleRange "(#$vehicleRange ?VEH ?DIST) means that ?DIST is the maximum distance that can be translated using the vehicle ?VEH, without intermediate refueling and assuming typical usage and normal operating parameters.  We intend this to be a very strict measure, an important thing to keep in mind since the vernacular sense of 'effective range' is much looser.  In point of fact, the #$vehicleRange is a key tool in calculating what the effective operating range of a fuel-powered vehicle is.  If, eg, we are dealing with a case of a vehicle that operates from a fixed base of operations, such as a #$FighterPlane, the effective operating range will ordinarily be one-half the absolute #$vehicleRange, since ordinarily provision will be made for the plane's returning to base.  However, we may well want to consider special cases where this provision is not made.  Conversely, in cases where aerial refueling is a possibility, the actual effective operating range will be some multiple of the #$vehicleRange, or may even be indefinite.") 
