(#$comment #$givesSupportToAgentOfCategory "(#$givesSupportToAgentOfCategory GIVER RECEIVER CATEGORY) means that GIVER gives some positive amount of support, of category CATEGORY, to RECEIVER. For example, (#$givesSupportToAgent #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$Egypt #$MilitarySupport) means that the US gives some positive amount of military support to Egypt. This predicate is the 'type-level' version of #$givesSupportToAgent, and so whenever an assertion with #$givesSupportToAgentOfCategory as arg zero is true, so will be some possible assertion with #$givesSupportToAgent as arg zero not, in general, be 'redundant with' the assertion using the latter predicate, as the latter will generally be more specific. This predicate is suited to making assertions about inter-agent support relationships in the presence of limited information either about the amount of support given, or about the criteria, in context, for a given amount of support counting as 'high', 'low' 'medium', and so forth. This predicate is also suited to formulating rules for which particular degrees of support are irrelevant.") 
