(#$comment #$transitiveViaArg "(#$transitiveViaArg PRED1 PRED2 INT) means that the INTth argument position of PRED1 is transitive with respect to PRED2.  This means if we have an axiom of the form (PRED1 . ARGS), it would be correct to also have another axiom of the form (PRED1 . ARGS-PRIME), where ARGS-PRIME is the same as ARGS except the INTth arg, X, is replaced by another term Y such that (PRED2 X Y).  For example, given (#$relationAllExists #$anatomicalParts #$Mammal #$Head-AnimalBodyPart) and  (#$transitiveViaArg #$relationAllExists #$genlPreds 1), the axiom (#$relationAllExists #$physicalParts #$Mammal #$Head-AnimalBodyPart) would be true.  See also #$transitiveViaArgInverse.") 
