(#$comment #$DiplomaticImmunity "Persons who have the status #$DiplomaticImmunity are, by virtue of their positions in the diplomatic corps of a country, not subject to arrest by authorities of the country to which they are posted.  Moreover, they are not subject to search or seizure of their possessions, nor are they obliged to pay taxes in the host state nor to fulfil military obligations.  Persons with #$DiplomaticImmunity in a host state also enjoy that status in intermediate states through which they travel.  #$DiplomaticImmunity is extended to diplomatic couriers and those who carry a diplomatic bag.  Diplomats, who have #$DiplomaticStatus, thereby have #$DiplomaticImmunity.  Generally, members of diplomats' immediate families have #$DiplomaticImmunity, even though they themselves are not diplomats.") 
