(#$comment #$incapacitates "(#$incapacitates CIRC FACTOR AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that, in state
of affairs CIRC, FACTOR causes AGENT to be certainly incapable of doing
actions that are instances of ACT_TYPE, i.e., FACTOR brings it about that
the #$derivedProbability in CIRC of the statement `A would be successful at
ACT_TYPE_TOKEN if she tried' is zero. Note that incapacitating factors
prevent, but preventing factors need not be incapacitating. Positive examples of this notion:
being locked in a closet incapacitates one to play tennis; being a
convicted felon incapacitates one to run for elective offices in most
U.S. states. Negative example: an appointment prevents, but doesn't
incapacitate, me from meeting you at 3pm.") 
