(#$comment #$GeoculturalRegion "A collection of places, a subset of #$GeographicalRegion. Each instance of this collection is a region, such as #$SouthEastAsia, #$Scandinavia, or #$CentralAmerica, where economic, cultural, political and/or religious ties make it natural to think of the area as a coherent whole. Non-examples would include #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, where there is only a geographical commonality shared by the areas subsumed by the region, or the area of #$Nicaragua and #$CostaRica combined, which does not by itself form a natural grouping, but is subsumed by the #$GeoculturalRegion #$CentralAmerica.  A final non-example: 'Spanish-speaking countries,' which do not form a single continuous area. The exact boundaries for such regions are sometimes difficult to determine, and sometimes it is unclear whether a region ought to count as one. Note that one country may be subsumed by more than one #$GeoculturalRegion: #$Norway is in both #$WesternEurope and #$Scandinavia.") 
