(#$comment #$GovernmentAffiliatedInformationDesignation "A subcollection of #$InformationDesignation.  Instances of
this collection are attributes of information.  Specifically, they are designations of information
that are, or could be, used by governments, coalitions that are formed between governments, or 
between a government and other political groups to specify the conditions under which information of interest 
or use to them can be accessed.  For instance, if a government contracted with the political group
Amnesty International for a foreign (or domestic) operation that required access to protected information,
they might designate such information in order to manage and enforce its application, accessibility, and use.
In this case, the designations of the information would be instances of #$GovernmentAffilitatedInformationDesignation. 
Note that the designation scheme might borrow from preexisting schemes that the government might already use, although it
could also include novel naming conventions to prevent mis-application and confusion about the scope of the
designations: 'Classified-AmnestySecret', 
for instance.") 
