(#$comment #$AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to denote the collection of           #$PurposefulActions in which some instance of a type of #$PhysicalDevice           is added to some instance of #$SystemOfDevices.             (#$AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn SYS DEVTYPE)           denotes the collection of #$Actions in which some instance of DEVTYPE is added           to SYS so that it can work together with the other members of SYS.  Note that           the #$resultGenls of this function includes #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.           What kind of #$Actions this subcollection           contains depends of course on what the type of #$SystemOfDevices SYS is.             If, for instance, SYS consists of instances of #$RadioTransmitter and           #$RadioReceiver, then the #$Actions that consist in adding to SYS may involve           no more than placing an instance of #$RadioReceiver in an appropriate           location and seeing to it that it is in working condition and can receive           a proper range of frequencies.            If SYS is an instance of #$TelephoneSystem, then the #$Actions that consist           in adding to SYS will likely be much more involved: all the actions that go           into hooking up a telephone.") 
