(#$comment #$SecondsDuration "Seconds are the standard unit of #$Time-Quantity in Cyc.  Think of #$SecondsDuration as a function; it takes one or two numbers and returns, as its value, some amount of #$Time-Quantity.   An expression of the form (#$SecondsDuration ?num) denotes a #$Time-Quantity that is exactly ?num seconds long.  An expression of the form (#$SecondsDuration ?min ?max) denotes a quantity of #$Time-Quantity that is at least ?min seconds at most ?max seconds long. Note:  Cyc's ontology contains ways to specify nonuniform distributions (e.g., a normal distribution with a mean and standard deviation), but for most purposes this simple uniform specification of `a piece of time' has proven itself to be the most useful building block.") 
(#$comment #$argGenl "(#$argGenl REL N COL) means that anything given as the Nth
argument to the Relationship REL must have the Collection
COL among their #$genls. Examples: (#$argGenl #$AtomFn 1 #$ElementStuff), (#$argGenl #$exports 2
#$Individual) and (#$argGenl #$argGenl 3 #$Thing). See also
#$arg1Genl, #$arg2Genl, #$arg3Genl, #$arg4Genl, #$arg5Genl, and #$arg6Genl
for predicates that more tersely state this constraint for the most
common argument positions.") 
