(#$comment #$PlanDynamicSituationMicrotheory "Instances of #$PlanDynamicSituationMicrotheory, or a specialization thereof, should be used for specifying the dynamic elements of the background situation relevant to some plan. Dynamic elements are those elements that are subject to relatively immediate change within the time interval that would subsume the plan, were it to be executed. For example, the location of a particular AGENT, just prior to the plan time, is a dynamic element of the background situation, as the agent can (presumably) change his location. The availability of non-durable provisions for use in executing a plan are also dynamic elements, since such provisions can be used up, or destroyed, etc. Static elements (e.g., geographical features) should be represented in an instance of #$PlanStaticSituationMicrotheory, or specializations thereof.") 
