(#$comment #$evidentialSupport "#$evidentialSupport AGENT INFO AMOUNT) means that the
evidence AGENT has bearing on the truth of INFO makes it reasonable to
have degree AMOUNT of belief in INFO. Roughly, this is to say that
there is some (possibly complex) proposition PROP such that (#$beliefs
AGENT PROP) and (#$conditionalProbability INFO PROP NUMBER), where
given the domain assumptions of the relevant Mt, NUMBER falls within
the range determined by the #$GenericQuantity AMOUNT (i.e.,
(#$inInterval NUMBER AMOUNT)). (#$evidentialSupport AGENT INFO AMOUNT)
does not mean that AGENT in fact does have degree of belief AMOUNT in
INFO; that is, it does not entail (#$confidenceLevel AGENT INFO
AMOUNT). arg3 is constrained to be an instance of #$GenericQuantity,
rather than of #$Real0-1, in order to make use of this predicate
feasible in practice (since we can often say of an agent that she has
a low, medium or high amount of evidence for a given proposition, but
can rarely or never say she has exactly N degree of evidence, for some
particular instance N of Real0-1). This predicate's main use is in
stating relations among propositional attitudes such as those
expressed by #$beliefs, #$knows, #$goals and so on; there
will probably be relatively few occasions to assert GAFs with
#$evidentialSupport as arg zero.") 
