argument is a proposition in which an #$ActionPredicate is used in the
arg 0 place. In other words, (effectOfAction-Props ?ACTION-PROP ?PROP)
means that the effect of ?ACTION-PROP, where ?ACTION-PROP is a
proposition of the form (?PRED .?ARGS) and ?PRED is an instance of
#$ActionPredicate, is ?PROP, where ?PROP is any proposition that
describes the effect(s) of ?ACTION-PROP.") 
