(#$comment #$isAContraryFactorFor "(#$isAContraryFactorFor CIRC FACTOR AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that, in
state of affairs CIRC, FACTOR would cause AGENT's likelihood of success in
doing actions that are tokens of ACT_TYPE to be lower, i.e., the
conditional probability of AGENT's succeeding at ACT_TYPE given FACTOR is
less than it would be if FACTOR did not obtain. In other words, FACTOR
brings it about that the #$derivedProbability in CIRC of the proposition
expressed by 'A would be successful at ACT_TYPE_TOKEN if she tried' is
decreased. Note that 'being a contrary factor' in this sense is
CIRC-relative: in the present, ordinary circumstances not having coffee
readily available might be a contrary factor for Julia to make a successful
presentation, but perhaps it would not be so if CIRC is a state of affairs
in which Julia has slept for 3 straight days and is fully rested.") 
