(#$comment #$inReactionTo "This is the weakest and most general of all the predicates dealing with 'reaction' or 'response' that incorporates an intentional component.  (#$inReactionTo ACT EVENT) entails that there be an AGENT with some goal such that AGENT believes EVENT changes the likelihood of the goal, and that one of the outcomes of this belief is ACT, which is performedBy AGENT (i.e., ACT is done deliberately).  This predicate does not cover cases of involuntary or instinctive reaction, for which a weaker sense of causation is appropriate.--Rode, Feb 17, 1998") 
