(#$comment #$NetDecreasingFunction "#$NetDecreasingFunction is function which shows a net decrease in its value from 'start' to 'finish'.  Such functions may take on any intermediate values so long as the net change in value from 'start' to 'finish' is negative.  More formally, let x denote an element in the domain of some #$NetIncreasingFunction, F.  Thus F(x) denotes an element in the range of F.  Let x1 denote the lower bound on x.  Let x2 denote the upper bound on x.  F is an #$NetDecreasingFunction if and only if F(x1) > F(x2).  See #$NetIncreasingFunction.  See also #$MonotonicallyDecreasingFunction whose elements show an increase (technically, a non-decrease) for each successive range element.") 
