(#$comment #$HighToVeryHigh "An instance of #$GenericQuantity.  #$HighToVeryHigh represents the attribute of having a high-to-very-high amount of some measurable but numerically unspecified quantity.  The interval
        represented by #$HighToVeryHigh subsumes amounts falling under \"greater than or
        equal to #$High\". Thus, if we were to create the quantities \"VeryVeryHigh\" and \"IncrediblyHigh\", both of those new quantities should
        have #$HighToVeryHigh as their #$genlAttributes. Like the other generic quantities, #$HighToVeryHigh may be used in connection with specialized predicates that indicate what is being measured; e.g., #$goalImportance, #$feelsTowardsObject, and
#$personalityAttributes.") 
