(#$comment #$EconomicEmbargo "The collection of events in which one nation, acting as an agent,
officially forbids all economic commerce with a particular country,
and takes additional steps to prevent and/or intercept all relevant
instances of commerce trade.  Often, but not always, embargoes are
cases of punishing or imposing sanctions.  An embargo can be thought
of as the most extreme possible case of imposing trade restrictions.
In CycL, we take an embargo to be the combination of the
legal/official edict interdicting commerce and the actual steps taken
to enforce the edict, eg, the conducting of additional customs
inspections in ports.") 
