(#$comment #$ClosedWorldAssumptionNote "#$minimizeExtent and #$minimizeExtentForArg are used to state weak closed-world assumptions.  They result in weak arguments (assumptions) for the negation of positive GAFs that can't be proven. #$completeExtentKnown, #$completeExtentKnownForArg and #$completeCollectionExtent are used to state strong closed-world assumptions.  They result in strong arguments for the negation of positive GAFs that aren't found by KB lookup.  Both types of predicates can be used within a specific Microtheory to say that that Mt (and all its spec-mts) should minimize, or restrict to known GAFs, the extent of the affected predicate.") 
