(#$comment #$GeographyMt "This #$Microtheory is for is for rules and assertions about #$Collections of geographical things and geographical predicates. It includes general information about geography and rules about types of #$GeopoliticalEntity without making any assertions about the #$PlanetEarth or any #$Individual on it.  Assertions about natural features of the Earth or
about instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity, treated as #$Agents, belong in #$WorldGeographyMt.  Those assertions which treat instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity as #$GeographicalRegions (e.g. stating that one #$City borders on a certain #$River) belong in #$WorldGeographyDualistMt.  If the assertions refer to objects in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, they belong in
the corresponding US-related microtheory (#$UnitedStatesGeographyMt or #$UnitedStatesGeographyDualistMt).  (See #$Dualist-Physical-AndGenericGeographyMtNote)") 
