(#$comment #$ArgumentTypeChecking-FORTSvsNonReifiedNATS "Arg-type checking imposes somewhat weaker constraints on non-reified function terms than it does for forts (first order reified terms).  Specifically, non-reified terms are required only to be consistent with arg-isa and arg-genls constraints using disjointness reasoning constraint is satisfied when no disjointness violation can be found. This is significantly weaker than the constraints imposed on forts: forts must provably satisfy applicable arg-isa and arg-genl constraints using isa and genls reasoning.") 
