(#$cyclistNotes #$orgFacilities "This is a stronger predicate than #$physicalQuarters,
in the sense that #$physicalQuarters does not imply the tight
'one-to-one' relation between the organization and the
facility/location that #$orgFacilities does.  On the other hand,
#$physicalQuarters also has a more restrictive arg-type in the second
argument position, namely #$ConstructionArtifact.  Since we want to be
able to talk about locations being #$orgFacilities, we do not want to
tighten the second argument constraint on the #$orgFacilities
predicate.  In the case where the #$orgFacilities of an organization
is given as a #$ConstructionArtifact, we shall infer that this is the
#$physicalQuarters of the organization in question.") 
