(#$comment #$wordForms "(#$wordForms WORD PRED STRING) states that STRING is a PRED form of WORD
in the current context, where PRED is an instance of #$SpeechPartPredicate.
For instance, in the #$EnglishMt and its spec-Mts, (#$wordForms #$Ox-TheWord
#$plural \"oxen\"); (#$wordForms #$Walk-TheWord #$pastTense \"walked\").
The code support for this predicate looks up irregular forms stated in
the KB -- such as (#$plural #$Ox-TheWord \"oxen\") -- and generates regular forms
such as \"walked\", which need not be stated in the KB.") 
