(#$cyclistNotes #$networkActualizes "Lurking at the back of this predicate there is probably a significant problem involving equivalence reasoning, that we are mostly deferring for now.  Put simply, when it is the case (#$networkActualizes IDEAL REAL), there is some sense that IDEAL and REAL both represent two possible characterizations of the same thing--and the sense, moreover, that IDEAL is probably in some sense counterfactual in the context of the assertion.  The predicate #$intraGroupSlotCorrespondsToLinkInSystem may be of some help to us here, in linking possible path systems to the #$Groups of which they are the potential characterizations.") 
