(#$comment #$relationAll "(#$relationAll PRED COL) means that, for every instance of COL (OBJ) the unary predicate PRED holds for OBJ. For example, the statement 'calendar dates are temporally continuous' can be represented as (#$relationAll #$temporallyContinuous #$Date).  Thus, #$relationAll can be used to express a whole class of rules about unary predicates as simple GAF assertions.  One must be aware of the implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ") 
