(#$cyclistNotes #$OfferingABribe "This new constant needs further fleshing out, esp. wrt the connection between bribing public officials (or company officers) (1) in order to gain influence with them and (2) (if the bribe's accepted, see #$TakingABribe) subsequently having influence with them. Bribery can remove legal obstacles to one's illicit activities.  For example, bribing a customs official not to inspect one's bag.  More generally, one may offer a bribe to an enforcement officer NOT to apply enforcement to oneself in a given situation in which the officer being bribed is the relevant authority (or representative of authority).") 
