(#$comment #$in-Permeates "(#$in-Permeates LIQUID SOLID)
means that LIQUID permeates SOLID.  LIQUID must be separable from SOLID
by physical, not chemical means.  LIQUID must be a #$LiquidTangibleThing, and SOLID a #$SolidTangibleThing.  If LIQUID is not a constituent (#$constituents) of SOLID, then SOLID is #$Porous.  Exemplars include water permeating a wet sponge (Sponge-CleaningImplement), #$Oil soaking a sponge,
or water in #$Soil.  Negative exemplars include vapor suspended in #$Air
(see, e.g. #$suspendingFluid or #$solute) .  Other negative exemplars
include liquids which undergo a chemical change and combine with some
other substance, e.g. water which becomes a chemical part of plant
material in photosynthesis.") 
