(#$comment #$goalProvidesMotiveFor "(#$goalProvidesMotiveFor GOAL AGT
ACT-TYPE ROLE) means that AGT's having the goal GOAL would provide her
with a motive for acting in the specified way -- i.e., for playing
ROLE in an instance of ACT-TYPE.  Note that (#$goalProvidesMotiveFor GOAL
AGT ...) does not entail that AGT actually has GOAL as a goal
-- only that, *if* she had this goal,
she would be credited (ordinarily) with having a motive for doing
some instance of ACT-TYPE. #$goalProvidesMotiveFor is a specialization
of #$providesMotiveFor which focuses on common motivational links
between #$goals and action-types. For further discussion concerning
the notion of 'motive' at work here, see the comment on
#$providesMotiveFor.") 
