(#$cyclistNotes #$testTimeElapsed "This information is good to store in the KB in order to allow flexible data utilization: if a constant is renamed, the data does not become impossible to retrieve, time elapsed comparisons can be done either immediately at test run time, or during a comparision done after an entire test suite run, arbitarily complex queries can be done without access to database software (e.g. 'show me queries showing a time difference of more than 5 percent which were exact hits in both runs and Okeefe was their #$testCyclistsResponsible can be done as an ask in cycl).  The risk of this constant is that needless data will acrete in the KB.  Killing unneeded elements of #$KBTestSuiteRun ameliorates this risk.  On the other hand, archival benchmark times might be useful to save every year or so.") 
