(#$comment #$infoPathway-Complete "The predicate #$infoPathway-Complete is used to indicate that the instance of          #$InformationBearingThing transferred in some instance of #$InformationTransferEvent follows the entire length of an         instance of #$Path-Spatial during the entire transfer.           (#$infoPathway-Complete TRANS PATH) means that the entire route of TRANS           is spatial and follows PATH.  By definition, any #$infoPathway-Complete of an
          instance of #$InformationTransferEvent connects the starting and stopping points
          (the #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination) of the entire instance
          (See also #$pathConnects).  Note: Compare #$infoPathway-Complete with
          #$infoPathway-Partial; the former refers to an instance of #$Path-Spatial containing the
          entire route of a particular instance of #$InformationTransferEvent.  A sub-region
          (shorter segment) of an #$infoPathway-Complete is NOT itself considered an
          #$infoPathway-Complete of the same #$InformationTransferEvent; i.e., if
          (#$infoPathway-Complete TRANS PATH) is true, and we cut PATH up into ten pieces
          PATH1, ..., PATH10, then it will generally not
          be true that (#$infoPathway-Complete MOVE PATH8), but it will be true that
