(#$comment #$cooperationLevel "(#$cooperationLevel COOP LEVEL) means that the cooperation level of the CooperationEvent COOP IS as described in LEVEL.  Here IS emphasize the time when the sentence (#$cooperationLevel COOP LEVEL) is evaluated since the level of the cooperation may change during the temporal extension of COOP.  Note that the LEVEL only has a relative value in the sense that only the comparison of different values (rather than the values themselves) has real meanings.  For example, a COOP may start from a small trade between two countries, followed by some official agreement of cooperation on some econimic projects, which in turn is followed by some military cooperation.  The level of cooperation increases in such an example from each stage to the next.") 
