(#$comment #$recipientOfInfo-Intended "The predicate #$recipientOfInfo-Intended is used to indicate who among those who receive information in a communication event were also intended to receive the information.  (#$recipientOfInfo-Intended COMM RECIPIENT) holds whenever (i) RECIPIENT                                        successfully receives the information communicated in the                                        communication event COMM (see #$recipientOfInfo) and                                       (ii) RECIPIENT is one of the #$Agents that the #$senderOfInfo in                                       the #$CommunicationAct-Single COMM intended to receive the information                                       (see #$communicationTarget).  For example, suppose I am speaking                                       at a closed meeting to one or more persons on classified                                       information                                        and, unbeknownst to me, a spy outside the room is listening in and hears everything                                       I am saying.  If each of the persons in the meeting hears everything                                       I am saying, then each bears the relation                                       #$recipientOfInfo-Intended to each instance of                                       #$CommunicationAct-Single COMM during the meeting of which I am the                                        #$senderOfInfo.  The spy, however, bears only the relation                                       #$recipientOfInfo to each of these instances.  Suppose, however, that                                       one person at the meeting is hard of hearing and does                                       not hear what I am saying.  Each event COMM is still a                                        #$CommunicationAct-Single since it had at least one                                       #$subEvents that is an instance of                                        #$AccessingAnIBT (at least the spy heard what was said) but the                                       person who is hard of hearing is a #$communicationTarget of COMM but not a                                       #$recipientOfInfo-Intended since he or she did not receive the                                       information, i.e. was not a #$recipientOfInfo.  See also #$intendedAudience.") 
