(#$cyclistNotes #$orgFacilities "Note that it is appropriate
to use this predicate just in case exactly one Organization is tied to
exactly one physical location by some sort of formal arrangement or
obligation, to the extent that it becomes appropriate to talk about
*the* organizational facilities of the organization, and, conversely,
about *the* organization that uses the facility.  I.e., if more than
one organization makes use of the same facility, or if more than one
facility is a facility of said organization, this is not the
appropriate relation to use. .  E.g., this is the relationship that
pertains between an #$AirportOrganization and its corresponding
#$Airport-Physical.  It is also the relationship that obtains between a
military unit and its 'posting' for the duration of the posting.") 
