(#$cyclistNotes #$DontSetDefaultAdvancedInferenceParametersNote "The fact that #$DontSetDefaultAdvancedInferenceParametersNote needs to be mentioned has #$BillJ concerned that this stuff has been ontoligized incorrectly.  He couldn't think of a better way to ontologize it around their creation time so decided that it was good enough.  But just now (27 March 2000) he has an idea that he and interested others should mull over...The idea is to do it as a set of unary predicates.  E.g.  reify the unary predicate 'enableUnboundPredicateRuleBackchain' but do not reify the defaults. So do not reify 'disableUnboundPredicateRuleBackchain'.  Instead minimize the predicates so that no assertion means use the system default value.  If contervening consideration comes in a few days consider that all of #$TestAdvancedInferenceParameterAttributes and #$testAdvancedInferenceParameters will be convereted into the unary predicate way of doing things.") 
