(#$comment #$CoalitionClassification-US "A subcollection of #$CoalitionInformationDesignation.
Instances of this collection are attributes.  Specifically, they are the attributes 
#$CoalitionClassificationUS-TopSecret, #$CoalitionClassificationUS-Secret, or 
#$CoalitionClassificationUS-Confidential.  These attributes are similar to the attributes in the collection
#$ClassificationUS (#$TopSecretInformation, #$SecretInformation, and #$ConfidentialInformation), but differ
in that they are applied only to information that is classified and accessible by a
selected members of those governments that comprise an active
coalition formed with the US.  Instances of this collection will not be applied 
to the same information that gets classified by
the US government, but rather to the sum of information that is
used, valued and deemed in need of protection by members of the coalition, although there may indeed be overlap.
Hence, at least some of the information classified using an instance of the collection #$Classification-US will not
be classified by using an instance of the collection #$CoalitionClassication-US, and likewise 
some of the information that gets classified using an instance of the collection #$CoalitionClassification-US will
not be classified using an instance of the collection 
#$Classification-US.  Note, however,
that instances of both collections will
share the US government's classification
scheme--'Confidential', 'Secret', and
'TopSecret'.") 
