(#$comment #$SystemicException "The mechanism is not violated but
rather, even though followed correctly, results in sub-optimal
behavior from a global perspective. This can be vewied as violation of
the agent to society contract (e.g. that the society is fair,
efficient, stable), and is fundamentally a result of suboptimal
coordination mechanism design.  Another possible view is that these
represent violations of safety properties i.e. violations of
constraints that something bad (e.g. thrashing, resource
over-utilization) will not happen.") 
