(#$comment #$intensionallyTransparent "A characteristic predicated of instances of both #$SituationTypeSlot and #$SituationTypePred-Ternary.  If (#$intensionallyTransparent PRED) and PRED is used to express a GAF where the 'sit type' argument is expressed as (#$CollectionSubsetFn #$Situation (#$TheSetOf FORMULA)) and FORMULA provably entails ENTFORMULA in CycL, then an analogous GAF holds for PRED in which the other argument or arguments are the same as before, and the 'sit type' argument is (#$CollectionSubsetFn #$Situation (#$TheSetOf ENTAILEDFORMULA)).  More collocquially, if a situation type pred is #$intensionallyTransparent and relates a #$SituationType with a certain definition to an argument or arguments, then it also relates any #$SituationType whose definitionis a generalization of the first to the same argument or arguments.") 
