(#$comment #$cospatial "(#$cospatial THING1 THING2) means that the #$SpatialThings THING1 and THING2 have the same spatial extent.  This doesn't imply that they are one and the same or have any parts in common, since we don't rule out that distinct things might spatially coincide or partially overlap without sharing any common parts.  For example, a shadow cast on a wall, and the surface of the wall; or a wall and the magnetic field surrounding an electrical outlet in the wall.  (As a further example, we might wish in some contexts to treat the visual images reflected in mirrors as localized things the public, external world; these images, then, would spatially intersect solid objects situated in back of a mirror without being part of them.)  See also #$spatiallySubsumes and #$spatiallyIntersects.") 
