(#$comment #$vulnerableTo "(#$vulnerableTo THREAT-OBJ OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that THREAT-OBJ poses harm of type HARM-TYPE to OBJECT.  It is important to note that the threat directed at OBJECT by THREAT-OBJ is somehow inherent to THREAT-OBJ and somewhat independent of the situation in which we find both of them.  This fact should be reflected in the choice of the third argument.  HARM-TYPE should characterize something THREAT-OBJ can do to OBJECT rather than a damage result to OBJECT.  For instance, (#$vulnerableTo Knife001 Person001 #$StabbingSomething) would be preferable to (#$vulnerableTo Knife001 Person001 #$IncurringAnInjury) since in the former case the HARM-TYPE is described as something the THREAT-OBJ does.") 
