(#$comment #$alongsidePathSegment "This predicate relates an object that is alongside a
customary path to the precise segment of the path that the 
object is strictly alongside.  The path segment will have
the same length as whichever dimension (if any) of the object
is aligned with the path.  More precisely, 
(#$alongsidePathSegment THING SEGMENT) means that SEGMENT is 
a #$subPaths of some PATH that THING is #$onPath-Alongside, 
and SEGMENT is the longest portion of PATH lying between two 
planes that both intersect THING and are both perpendicular 
to the centerline of PATH.  For example, a 100-foot-wide 
building standing alongside and facing a street is 
#$alongsidePathSegment the corresponding 100-foot-long 
segment of the street.") 
