(#$comment #$WagingAColdWar "An instance of #$WagingAColdWar is an 
intense rivalry between two or more countries 
in areas of diplomacy, economic strategy,
 and military preparation, falling just
 short of armed conflict.  However, it must
 be kept in mind that #$subEvents of cold wars
 can be full-fledged
 armed conflicts.  Such conflicts might involve
one or more
 of the countries waging the cold war, as well
  as other countries whose participation
 in the armed conflict serves some of the ends of the
  aforementioned countries.  So, for example,
  the #$VietnamWar, while a genuine 'hot' war, 
was a subEvent
  of the cold war between the U.S. and the
  U.S.S.R.") 
