(#$comment #$testQuestionEnglish "(#$testQuestionEnglish TEST ENGLISH) means that ENGLISH is one possible english question which corresponds to the system functionality described by TEST.  ENGLISH is the sort of thing that we would want to enter into the 'Query Text' box of the Tell/Ask Prototype.  Corresponding #$testQuestionEnglish and #$testQuestionCycL assertions (as well as #$testScenarioEnglish #$testScenarioCycL) assertions can be used as targets for our natural language interpreter.  Note that certain sub-classes of #$TestQuestionMicrotheory are less appropriate for said targeting task.  E.g. #$testQuestionEnglish for most elements #$HPKB-Y1-CM-SQ-Microtheory is inappropriate for any near term (Feb '98) NL to CycL interpretation work.  On the other hand #$ImageDemoTestMicrotheory and #$NLInterpretationTest are the sorts of things for which NL team is more likely to be working on in the near term (Nov '98).  However, if one is specifying nl focused test suites (see #$NLInterpretationTest), then #$testEnglish has now (Mar 2000) replaced #$testQuestionEnglish as the correct predicate to use.") 
