(#$comment #$suspendedIn "(#$suspendedIn OBJ FLUID) means that OBJ is fully immersed in FLUID, and OBJ is suspended in FLUID.  In other words, OBJ does not undergo rapid falling or rising due to its relative density.  Although forces such as convection currents in FLUID may cause OBJ to rise or fall, net buoyancy forces acting on OBJ are near zero.  Note that while #$suspendedIn correctly describes the condition of a #$suspendedPart in its #$suspendingFluid (e.g., a dirt particle suspended in water), #$suspendedIn can also be used more broadly (e.g., a hot air balloon is #$suspendedIn air).  See also #$Suspension.  An underwater bubble floating to the surface is a negative exemplar usage of #$suspendedIn because it is rising.  The bubble is #$in-ImmersedFully the water, however.  See also #$in-Floating to describe objects which are at the surface of a liquid.") 
