(#$comment #$DecidingWhichInstrumentPredicateToUse "Which instrument predicate you use depends on what level of generality you wish your statement to apply at.  One help is to look at the argument types of each instrument predicate and decide.  Do you want it to apply to every #$PartiallyTangible which is an instrument?  Then use #$instrument-Generic since #$PartiallyTangible is its #$arg2Isa.  Are you writing a rule which really only applies to #$PhysicalDevices  Then use #$deviceUsed.  But be careful!  When you use a more specific predicate such as #$deviceUsed it may have special extra conditions in its definition aside from the #$PhysicalDevice #$arg2Isa constraint.  Also if your first stab at the rule involves #$deviceUsed in the antecedent, see if it applies more generally to #$instrument-Generic.") 
