(#$comment #$ApplicationLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols that
implement an application layer.
A user interacts directly with an instance of #$ApplicationLayerProtocol, 
so it is the top layer in a #$NetworkProtocolStack. In an instance of
#$OpenSystemInterconnectionReferenceModel, an #$ApplicationLayerProtocol communicates 
with a #$PresentationLayerProtocol. In most other models, it communicates with a
#$TransportLayerProtocol.") 
