(#$comment #$interArgResultReln "(#$interArgResultReln FUNC N RELN) means that a NAT using FUNC (in the former's arg0 position) denotes something RESULT that stands in the #$BinaryPredicate RELN to the thing ARGN appearing in FUNC's Nth argument position within the NAT, with ARGN appearing as the first argument of
RELN and RESULT appearing as the second argument of RELN.  That is, if 
(FUNC ARG1...ARGN...) = RESULT, then (RELN ARGN RESULT) is true.  For example,
(#$interArgResultReln #$SubPathInsideRegionFn 1 #$subPaths) means that the
result of applying #$SubPathInsideRegionFn to a given PATH and REGION is a 
#$subPaths of PATH. See also #$interResultArgReln.") 
