(#$comment #$consistent "(consistent F) means that the 
formula F is consistent with the outer context in which 
the #$consistent statement is made. For instance, the 
formula   (#$consistent       
(#$thereExists ?CLOSURE         (#$and           
(#$isa ?CLOSURE #$BlockingAnInternationalWaterway)           
(#$performedBy ?CLOSURE #$Iran)           
(#$objectActedOn ?CLOSURE #$StraitOfHormuz)))) 
means that is consistent with the other information 
(in the mt in which this is asserted) to say that Iran blocks the Strait of Hormuz. Obviously, this is not the same as saying that Iran actually does so. ") 
