(#$comment #$Judaism "One of the oldest religions practiced in the world today, the origins
of Judaism can be traced back as far as the Bronze Age.  Judaism is
characterized by its assertion of the unity of God (monotheism), the
justice and morality of God, and the claim that a special covenant
exists between God and the Jewish nation.  It is also characterized by
a rigorous legal and moral code which together with sources like the
code of Hammurabi and Greek and Roman law has been a fundamental
influence on the Western legal tradition.") 
