(#$comment #$ordersTroopMovement "(ordersTroopMovement ORDERER ORDEREE FROM) means that the commanding officer, ORDERER, orders the subordinate unit, ORDEREE, to prepare to move out from the location FROM. Note that unit may not yet be in the FROM location at the time of the order. Hence, (objectFoundInLocation is not ORDEREE FROM) is not a precondition for this action. (objectFoundInLocation ORDEREE FROM) is, however, an effect, since having been order to move out from FROM, the unit will presumably move into FROM in preparation for carrying out the order.") 
