(#$cyclistNotes #$vulnerableTo "(5/2000) Some contention remains over the use of this predicate.  It is arguable that all vulnerabilities are situational and (hence) that the predicate should make reference to the situation.  Second, it is not clear that the distinction between the various harm types is ultimately defensible, and unless we can be clearer about the harm type distinctions we run the risk of perpetuating documented requirements that will be violated in the KB.  I propose that we address these questions in turn, and in the meantime understand #$vulnerableTo as hiding the implicit situation in which THREAT-OBJ (#$instrument-Generic?) acts on OBJECT (#$objectActedOn?).") 
