(#$comment #$pathEndsInRegion "This predicate relates a spatial path to a spatial region inside of which the path ends.  (#$pathEndsInRegion PATH REGION)
means that there is a #$subPaths of PATH that contains one of 
PATH's #$endsOfPathSegment and is #$pathInsideRegion REGION 
(as a limiting case, the path end might be #$onLine REGION's 
border).  PATH might or might not be a #$subPaths of some 
SUPERPATH that does not end inside REGION; so it does _not_ 
follow from the above formula that REGION contains a 
#$pathTerminus (q.v.) of PATH.") 
