(#$cyclistNotes #$DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn "There is an asymmetry between the function #$AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn                and its cousin #$DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn.  In the latter,                it is asserted that every instance of the result of applying the                function to allowable arguments has, as a #$subEvents, an                instance of #$RemovingSomething.  In instances of #$RemovingSomething,                the #$objectRemoved can be removed by being destroyed or                it can be removed by ways in which it still exists afterwards.                Thus, an instance of #$RemovingSomething may also be a                 #$DestructionEvent or it may also be simply an instance                of #$TransferOut.  For the function #$AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn, I                could find no analogue to #$RemovingSomething.  So I have                asserted only that every instance of the result of applying                this function to allowable arguments has, as a #$subEvents, an                instance of #$TransferIn.") 
