(#$comment #$Anthropacity "#$Anthropacity is a class of #$AttributeValues which are used to organize the #$Microtheory structure in Cyc.  If a microtheory has a very general #$Anthropacity value, it assumes less about the existence of a physical universe, living things, and so on. Microtheories which have more specific, detailed, or `dense' #$Anthropacity values are assumed to be `about' civilized people living on Earth.  Relative generality (specificity) is indicated by the predicate #$genlAttributes.  (#$genlAttributes ATTRIBUTE-1 ATTRIBUTE-2) means that in a nested hierarchy of values including ATTRIBUTE-1 and ATTRIBUTE-2, ATTRIBUTE-2 is more general than ATTRIBUTE-1.  If a particulary microtheory has an anthropacity of ATTRIBUTE-1, this entails that it also has a (more general) anthropacity of ATTRIBUTE-2.  See also #$mtAnthropacity.") 
