(#$comment #$TreeOrdering "The collection of all those #$PartialOrderings ORDER in which the ordering relation R orders elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER into a tree-like structure.  This means that each pair of elements of S has a common 'R-lower-bound' in S (i.e., for each X, Y in S, there is a Z in S such that R(Z X) and R(Z Y)), and the set of 'R-lower-bounds' of each X in S is ordered in a chain by R (i.e., {Y: Y is in S and R(Y X)} is a chain).  Note that a #$TreeOrdering can itself be a chain, i.e., a #$TotalOrdering.  Note also that if you want a #$RelationalStructure that is just like a #$TreeOrdering but with the ordering relation to be irreflexive, see #$TreeOrdering-Strict.") 
