(#$comment #$DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to denote the collection of           #$PurposefulActions in which some instance of a type of #$PhysicalDevice           is deleted from or taken out of some instance of #$SystemOfDevices.             (#$DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn SYS DEVTYPE)           denotes the subcollection of #$Actions in which some           instance of DEVTYPE is taken out of           from SYS.  What kind of #$Actions this subcollection           contains depends of course on what the type of #$SystemOfDevices SYS is.             If, for instance, SYS consists of instances of #$RadioTransmitter and           #$RadioReceiver, then the #$Actions that consist in deleting from SYS may involve           no more than destroying some instance of #$RadioTransmitter or taking it           out of range of all the instances of #$RadioReceiver in SYS.            If SYS is an instance of #$TelephoneSystem, then the #$Actions that consist           in deleting from SYS may be as simple as unplugging the telephone           or as complicated as whatever a telephone company does when it cuts           off someone's telephone service.") 
