(#$comment #$vulnerableToType "(#$vulnerableToType THREAT-OBJ-TYPE OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that instances of the collection THREAT-OBJ-TYPE generally pose harm results of type HARM-TYPE to OBJECT.  The purpose of this predicate is to represent the knowledge that an entire class of things poses a certain kind of vulnerability to a particular object.  For restrictions on the use of HARM-TYPE see #$vulnerableTo.  Note that this is a type-level predicate in the first argument place and that care needs to be taken in developing rules that draw #$vulnerableTo conclusions from #$vulnerableToType GAFs so that we do not overpopulate the KB with potentially questionable #$vulnerableTo judgments.") 
