(#$comment #$conflictLevel "(#$conflictLevel CONF LEVEL) means that the conflict level of the ConlictEvent CONF IS as described in LEVEL.  Here IS emphasize the time when the sentence (#$conflictLevel CONF LEVEL) is evaluated since the level of the conflict may change during the temporal extension of CONF.  Note that the LEVEL only has a relative value in the sense that only the comparison of different values (rather than the values themselves) has real meanings.  For example, a CONF may start from a radom shooting on the border between two countries, followed by some threats of using military force, which in turn is followed by a small battle at the border, which eventually results in a war.  The level of conflict increases in this example from each stage to the next.") 
