(#$comment #$groupAccountForFile "(#$groupAccountForFile FILE GROUP) means that the owner of FILE is a member of a user group GROUP on a computational system.  The owner of the file can determine whether members of his or her group have has read, write, or execute permissions on FILE.  (Note: the owner of a file is in the group qua network, but it is not in the group qua permission, i.e., it is possible for the #$permissionMode on a file to allow group access but not owner access.) The notable exception is the person who #$hasRootAccount, who can read, write, or execute any file on the network regardless of the permissions.  Setting up group accounts is one way to reduce the damage a hacker can do to computer network, because someone who breaks into a user's account will be able to access immediately only those files in the user's group, not all the files on the system.") 
