(#$comment #$relationAllExists "(#$relationAllExists SLOT COL1 COL2) means that, for every instance of COL1 (INS1), there is some instance of COL2 (INS2) such that (SLOT INS1 INS2) holds.  #$relationAllExists is thus redundant with a huge set of commonly-occurring rules.  By having this predicate (along with an axiom defining it, and, eventually, coded support for quick inferencing with it), those rules can be stated more tersely and reasoning at the collection level is possible.") 
(#$comment #$TaskAndOpAssociatesMt "The holding microtheory for test assertions concerning
'typical' association of task types with operation types in COAs. For
the present (4/99) this microtheory inherits from the
ModernMilitaryTacticsMt; it does *not* at present inherit to the
BattlespaceMilitaryMt, so that critiquing questions and test questions
that need this information will have to be given explicit access to
it. If results are sufficiently encouraging and the rules are deemed
sufficiently, valid, we will give the BattlespaceMilitaryMt access via
a genlMt linkage, and have all of the COA representations inherit this
information. ") 
