(#$cyclistNotes #$DontSetDefaultAdvancedInferenceParametersNote "If an #$TestAdvancedInferenceParameterAttribute is the system default, then there is almost never a need to set the value of #$testAdvancedInferenceParameters.  The default values (as of March 2000) are #$DisableHLPredicateBackchaining, #$EnableCacheBackwardQueryResults, #$DisableNegationByFailure, #$DisableUnboundPredicateRuleBackchain.  Thus for any of one those attributes, ATTRIBUTE, for any #$TestQuestionMicrotheory, it would almost never be necessary to assert (#$testAdvancedInferenceParameters TEST ATTRIBUTE).  Technicality: Here is a case when you would want to assert the local values: Suppose you were a lisp coder and you had clet-ed one of these parameters.  Inside of this clet you were doing a batch test run.  Suppose that for a particular test in this batch run, you wanted to override the clet'ed value.  In that case, it might make sense to use one of the above attribute settings.  Also, note that there is a way of overriding even the value specified by #$testAdvancedInferenceParameters for TEST.  See the optional arguments to run-kb-test.") 
