(#$comment #$ActionPredicate "#$ActionPredicate is a collection of predicates which are used to make assertions about actions performed by agents. An assertion made using an #$ActionPredicate, made in the context of a PlanningDomainMicrotheory, results in an open formula that may or may not be satisfied in some 'real world microtheory' - i.e., in a #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory. In the context of a #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory, an #$ActionPredicate is an ELRelation, and an assertion made using such a predicate results in the skolemization of an action of the type corresponding (see correspondingCycTerm) to the predicate in question. The skolemized action then serves as the first argument to a series of in that situation microtheory that involve #$ActorSlot predicates. For example, in a planning domain for some military operation, one might assert (blocks-Military FRIENDLY-UNIT HOSTILE-UNIT LOCATION). This would result in the following #$expansion: (thereExists ?BLOCK (and (isa ?BLOCK Block-MilitaryTask) (performedBy ?BLOCK FRIENDLY-UNIT) (objectActedOn ?BLOCK HOSTILE-UNIT) (prevents-SitProp ?BLOCK (traverses HOSTILE-UNIT ?FROM ?TO ?VIA-PATH)))).") 
