(#$comment #$cultureCoreParticipants "This predicate is a specialization of #$cultureParticipants that relates persons (and, potentially, other
  animals) to the cultures that they participate in in a central way.  (#$cultureCoreParticipants CULTURE PARTICIPANT) 
  means that PARTICIPANT is one of the primary #$socialParticipants in 
  the complex instance of #$SocialOccurrence that is CULTURE.  
  Core participation in a given culture implies possession of the qualities that the culture is defined in terms of, and implies strong tendencies toward certain 
  characteristic beliefs and practices of that culture (see #$cultureBeliefs and 
  #$culturePractices).  For example, although it is not necessarily the case that all #$cultureParticipants in teenage culture are actually in their teens,
this is the case for all of that culture's #$cultureCoreParticipants.") 
