(#$comment #$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn "A function that, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a node X in SYS as in (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn X SYS), returns the set of all links in SYS that X is on, i.e., the set of all links LINK in SYS such that (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) for some Y.  Note that if SYS is a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem and X is a node in SYS, then (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn X SYS) equals the union of (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS) and (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS) (these two sets will overlap if there are any 'bidirected' links at that node).  Note also that (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn X SYS) = #$TheEmptySet if there is no link in SYS that is between X and another node in SYS.  Loops, if any, are not included as links.") 
