(#$cyclistNotes #$SlotValueChangingFn "There are a couple of constraints to observe in using this function.  The second argument of the function must always be a permissable first argument for the slot given as the first argument of the function.  Since the #$arg2Isa of the function is #$SomethingExisting, we are effectively ruling out quantity slots that do not allow #$SomethingExistings in the first argument.  Similarly, the #$ScalarIntervals given as the third and fourth arguments of the function must be of a type that is actually allowable for the second argument of the slot given as the first argument of the function.  Finally, the third and fourth arguments should be different individuals.  At present (13 Jan 2000) these constraints are not explicitly enforced on Cyc assertions.") 
