(#$cyclistNotes #$nothingBetweenOfType "It has been suggested that we should add the condition that THING itself be an instance of COL.  However, this is something that probably should be resisted for the present.  In the first place, it constitutes a strange way of smuggling #$isa assertions into the KB.  Also, there is nothing declaratively in place to insure that what is asserted in the second argument position really is an instance of the collection cited.  If one wishes to assert that 'THING is the closest thing to REFERENT of type COL on the side of REFERENT that thing is on', use (#$and (#$isa THING COL) (#$nothingBetweenOfType REFERENT THING COL)).") 
