(#$comment #$distributesOutOfArg "(distributesOutOfArg <reln> <pred> <n>) is a directive to the canonicalizer 

that relation <reln> distrbutes out of a predicate <pred> when it appears as 

the top-most relation in the predicate's arg <n>.  Specifically, it denotes

(distributesOutOfArg <reln> <pred> <n>) denotes that the canonicalizer

will translate

(<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> (<reln> <arg-n1> <arg-n2> ... <arg-nm>) <arg-n+1> ..) 

into

(<reln> (<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-n1> <arg-n+1> ...) 

        (<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-n2> <arg-n+1> ...)

         ...

        (<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-nm> <arg-n+1> ...))") 
