(#$comment #$purposeOfSocialEvent "This predicate can be used to represent the goal in those
instances of #$SocialOccurrence that exist
so that participants in them can reach some particular goal.
(#$purposeOfSocialEvent EVENT FORMULA) means that the goal of
EVENT (as determined by at least
one participant in EVENT) is represented by FORMULA.
When EVENT is an instance of #$CooperationEvent, all 
#$cooperatingParticipants in EVENT
have the goal represented by FORMULA and are participating
in EVENT because they believe doing so will help
bring about that goal.
This predicate is particularly useful in connection with
instances of #$CooperationEvent
but can also be relevant for other subcollections of
#$SocialOccurrence, such as #$MilitaryExercise, 
#$HelpingAnAgent or #$BusinessEvent.") 
