(#$cyclistNotes #$cooperatingParticipants "In creating this predicate I had to decide between two distinct
meanings.  The narrower meaning is stated above in the #$comment.
A broader meaning would allow an agent to be a #$cooperatingParticipants 
  in a cooperation event merely by contributing willingly and causally to
  the achievement of the goal of the event, without necessarily participating 
  in the event for the sake of achieving this goal.  
For instance, construction workers
may participate in building a road, not for the sake of obtaining
a completed road, but for the sake of a paycheck.  Soldiers may
participate in a military operation, not for the sake of the 
goals of the operation but, again, to receive money or for other
personal reasons.
I have gone with the narrower meaning because this allows me to
better fill out the meaning of #$CooperationEvent and
#$partnersInCooperation.  At some point, however, we may want to
go with the broader meaning or create a new predicate that
captures this meaning. #$Meyer, August, 2000.") 
