(#$comment #$frontLineOfTroops "(frontLineOfTroops MILITARYFORCE ZONE) means that the #$ModernMilitaryOrganization MILITARYFORCE has deployed troops in a #$Battle, a campaign, or in a defensive position, and those troops have an outermost line or narrow ZONE in which troops are located at the edge of the maximal area controlled by MILITARYFORCE.  The ZONE is an abstract, possibly moving, #$GeographicalThing-Intangible-MovableLocation.  The front line of one force may coincide with or overlap the enemy's front line, or there may be a 'no-man's land' area separating them.  In certain formations, especially in high-speed, cavalry, guerilla or commando operations, there is often no identifiable zone that could be called the #$frontLineOfTroops of the force.") 
