(#$comment #$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation "(#$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation OBJ-TYPE PRED SIT-TYPE) means that when an INST1 of ?OBJ-TYPE is related via the binary predicate PRED to some second instance INST2, hardships of type SIT-TYPE propagate from INST1 to INST2.  Although ?INST1 and ?INST2 do not have to be the same kind of thing.  For instance, security weaknesses generally propagate through connected computer systems linked in certain ways, that is, if one computer is vulnerable to being attacked in a certain way so are others connected to it.  We would represent one version of this as (#$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation #$ComputationalSystem #$equivalentHosts #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity).") 
