(#$comment #$vulnerabilityCascades "(#$vulnerabilityCascades SOURCE-TYPE OBJ-TYPE RESULT-TYPE) means that in cases where an instance of SOURCE-TYPE makes an instance of OBJ-TYPE vulnerable to results of type RESULT-TYPE, the vulnerability transfers across other instances of SOURCE-TYPE and OBJ-TYPE.  In practical terms this means that every instance of OBJ-TYPE will be vulnerable to (or in) every instance of SOURCE-TYPE.  It also means that one should take *extreme* care in making assertions with #$vulnerabilityCascades.  Typical examples will be conceptually true.") 
