(#$comment #$subCapacities "(#$subCapacities CAPACITY SUBCAPACITY) means
 that SUBCAPACITY is subsumed under the greater or more comprehensive 
 CAPACITY.  That is, having CAPACITY entails having SUBCAPACITY, but not
 vice versa.  For example, the capacity to use a plan might be a subcapacity
 of being a problem solver.  The collection #$AgentCapacity is 
 ''well-founded'' in that there are some basic capacities that are not 
 subcapacities of any others (save themselves).") 
