(#$comment #$equalSymbols "(#$equalSymbols X Y) is true only when X and Y are identical symbols. Note that this is stronger than merely saying
that the the two symbols pick
           out the same individual or class of individuals, e.g.,
 'Bertrand Russell' and 'the author of
  'On Denoting''  both pick out the same individual, but are
           different symbols. Two symbols can even be identical in
           meaning and yet still be different symbols; e.g., 'bachelor'
           and 'unmarried male.' What would be #$equalSymbols
are 'bachelor' and 'bachelor.' ") 
