(#$comment #$traversalInSystem-OrderObserved "(#$traversalInSystem-OrderObserved TRAV SYS) means that TRAV is a #$Traversal of some paths in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, which observes the orders or directions of links (and paths) in SYS. To say that TRAV observes the orders or directions of links in SYS, we mean that for each link LINK in SYS between X and Y, (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X LINK Y)) is a subtraversal of TRAV only if (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds, and for each subpath SUB between A and B of a link LINK in SYS between X and Y, (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList A SUB B)) is a subtraversal of TRAV only if (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds.") 
