(#$comment #$vulnerableIn "(vulnerableIn SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that when in situation SITUATION, existing object OBJECT is vulnerable to hardships of type RESULT-TYPE.  The purpose of #$vulnerableIn is to represent vulnerabilities that stem from being in a particular situation, and presumably from playing some sort of role in that situation.  It is the situation taken as a whole, including the important background conditions, that pose the vulnerability, not some object exclusively.  Given this sense of vulnerability, and so as to distinguish this predicate from #$vulnerableTo and the like, we characterize RESULT-TYPE from OBJECT's perspective.  RESULT-TYPE should therefore be a 'passive' term.") 
