(#$comment #$InstantiationInstanceFn "#$InstantiationInstanceFn is intended to enable the user to take a predicate that is type-level in one or more of its argument positions, and create an analogous predicate that is instance level in one or more of those same positions.  More specifically, where TYPE-PRED is a predicate that takes #$Collections in arguments {N...M} and SET is a subset of {N...M}, (#$InstantiationInstanceFn TYPE-PRED SET) returns a predicate INST-PRED of the same #$arity as TYPE-PRED and such that, for every #$PositiveInteger ARGN that is an #$elementOf SET, (#$argIsa INST-PRED ARGN COL) is true if (#$argGenl TYPE-PRED ARGN COL) is true, and such that the argument constraints of any argument positions whose sequence numbers are not known to appear in SET are the same as the argument constraints on the corresponding argument positions for TYPE-PRED.  So, for example, it is true that (#$rewriteOf #$organismCanLethallyInfect (#$InstantiationInstanceFn #$organismTypeCanLethallyInfect (#$TheSet 1))).") 
