(#$comment #$TestStatusAttribute "Elements are descriptors of how an element of #$TestQuestionMicrotheory is working, either according to some person (use #$testStatus-Manual) or according to a some particular run of some testing code (use #$testStatus-Automatic.)  For example, are all of the target bindings being returned when the ask associated with TEST01Mt is called?  If the answer was yes for RunOfKBTestsOnTuesday then testing code should assert (#$testStatus-Automatic TEST01Mt RunOfKBTestsOnTuesday #$Hit-Exact).  Many of the commonly used elements of this collection such as #$MissedSome, #$FalsePositives, #$Hit-InExact and #$ErrorsOut are automatically computed by periodically run testing code.  Others such as #$InferencePathHasBeenFormulated or #$QueryHasBeenFormulated, are often subjective and are thus impossible to compute automatically in all cases.") 
