(#$cyclistNotes #$typicalFacilityOfOrgType "This predicate is weaker than #$orgTypeFacilityType in
that (#$orgTypeFacilityType ORG-TYPE PLACE-TYPE) means that every
instance of ORG-TYPE has exactly one instance of PLACE-TYPE that is
THE #$orgFacilities of the organization.  (#$typicalFacilityOfOrgType
ORG-TYPE PLACE-TYPE) merely says that under normal circumstances, an
instance of ORG-TYPE can be expected to control one or more instances
of PLACE-TYPE as 'facilities'--one of which may be the #$orgFacilities
of the organization, or it may not.  We do take it to be the case that
#$orgTypeFacilityType is a specpred of #$typicalFacilityOfOrgType.") 
