(#$comment #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate "A collection of predicates; the subset of #$BinaryPredicate whose elements represent reflexive relations. A predicate F is an element of #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate if and only if F is a binary predicate, and for every X in the domain of F, (F X X). Examples: #$subSeries, #$inRegion, #$genls, and #$equals. Note this additional restriction: A Cyc predicate F can be an element of #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate only if the type (i.e., arg-Isa) constraint applicable to F's first argument is not disjoint with the type constraint applicable to F's second argument. See also #$NoteOnArgumentTypingAndPropertiesOfRelations.") 
