(#$comment #$testAnswersEnglish "Values are answers that we would expect back from #$Cyc in something like the Tell/Ask Prototype.  In some cases, there is an answer that we would expect back in the short term (perhaps days to months), and a more sophisticated answer that we would expect in the longer term (perhaps months to years.).  In these cases one should put the long-term desired answer in brackets i.e. [ and ].  For example, suppose for a hypothetical example, the #$testQuestionEnglish for FooTestMt was 'If a car is going south is it going forward?'.  The short term answer is 'Yes'.  For the longer term we'd want an answer such as 'Probably yes since cars usually go forward when they are driven.'  The way to indicate this would be to use [ and ] like so: (#$testAnswersEnglish FootMt ''Yes [Probably yes since cars usually go forward when they are driven.]'').  Testing code which compares Cyc's answers against answers targeted by #$testAnswersEnglish will 'know' to disregard text that is found between [ and ].") 
