(#$comment #$Kirkuk-CeyhanPipeline "This #$Pipeline, 
also known as the Iraqi Turkish  
pipeline, is Iraq's largest operable crude
export pipeline.  It actually consists of two
parallel lines: a 40-inch line with a design capacity of 1.1
million b/d, and a 46-inch line with a design capacity of 
500,000 b/d.  As of late 1996 the combined operational 
capacity was in the range of 700,000 - 1,000,000 b/d.
Together they run from the #$CityOfKirkukIraq in Northern #$Iraq
to the #$CityOfCeyhanTurkey in the Mediterranean region of #$Turkey (EIA pages).") 
