(#$comment #$evaluateAtEL "(#$evaluateAtEL <functor>) directs the canonicalizer to translate each evaluatable
 expression involving <functor> into the evaluation value of the expression; e.g.,
 were (#$evaluateAtEL #$PlusFn) true in an mt, then the term (#$PlusFn 2 3 4) would
 canonicalize as 9 in that mt.  An EL evaluatable expression requires that all nested
 evaluatable expressions must be EL evaluatable; for example 
 (#$PlusFn 2 (#$DifferenceFn 3 4)) would not canonicalize as 1 in an mt unless both
 (#$evaluateAtEL #$PlusFn) and (#$evaluateAtEL #$DifferenceFn) were true in the mt.") 
