(#$comment #$providesMotiveFor "(#$providesMotiveFor INDIV AGT SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that INDIV
provides AGT with a motive for acting in the specified way -- i.e.,
for playing ROLE in an instance of SIT-TYPE.  INDIV will typically be
a #$Situation or a state of affairs (expressed by a #$CycFormula). Note
that this predicate does not take a particular action as its third
argument. It is *not* used to specify AGT's motive for participating
in some actual event (for this, use #$purposeInEvent or
#$reasonForAction). Also, note that one can have a 'motive' to do A
without ever having the corresponding goal or desire to do it. E.g.,
AGT might have a motive to kill his business partner (perhaps being
cheated in a business deal) even if AGT never actually desires to do
this. This is one sense of 'motive' discussed in criminal law contexts
-- INDIV provides AGT with a *reason* to play ROLE in SIT-TYPE, i.e.,
is the sort of event which often does and/or which reasonably could
lead an agent to do this.") 
