(#$comment #$statusInConflictEvent "(#$statusInConflictEvent AGENT EVENT STATUS) means that the #$Agent AGENT has the given #$ConflictEventStatus STATUS in the #$ConflictEvent EVENT.  An example of this would be (#$statusInConflictEvent #$DenverBroncos SuperBowl33-SecondQuarter #$Winning), which says that the Denver Broncos were winning Super Bowl XXXIII during the quarter mentioned. Statements ascribing an attribute to an agent will in most cases need to be explicitly temporally qualified.  The example given is an exception, because the #$DenverBroncos held #$Winning status throughout the entire second quarter.  If we wanted to assert that the Broncos were winning at some particular time during Super Bowl XXXIII, we would use #$holdsIn or #$holdsSometimeDuring to make explicit when the claim is true.") 
