(#$comment #$HumanActivitiesMt "The statements about actions in this microtheory are true regardless of whether the action is performed by a person or by organizations of people.  If an assertion is only true for actions performed by individual persons, it should go in the #$IndividualHumanActivitiesMt or one of the mts for which it is base; if an assertion is only true for actions performed by organizations, it should go in the #$OrganizationMt or one of its related mts.  The #$HumanActivitiesMt also includes the assumption that the people are not innovative in the way they perform the actions (e.g. tools are used for their intended purpose and nothing else, so no one would unlock a door with a credit card).  This microtheory assumes in addition that agents are rational, that they are aware of relevant aspects of their situation (e.g., aware of the capabilities they have for doing what they are doing), and that tools work the way they are supposed to.") 
