(#$comment #$physicallyCapableOf "'(#$physicallyCapableOf AGENT SIT-TYPE ROLE)' means that AGENT can physically play ROLE in a situation of SIT-TYPE.  This does not imply that AGENT is capable of doing so in the sense of know-how (see 
#$skillCapableOf), nor does it mean that AGENT has the resources to do so (see
#$resourceCapableOf).  For instance, (#$anatomicallyCapableOf 
#$MarthaThePassengerPigeon #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy), but if Martha were
caged, then (#$not (#$physicallyCapableOf #$MarthaThePassengerPigeon 
#$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)).  Similarly, if Martha's feet were stuck in
lime, she would also not be physically capable of flying.  It is this sense of 
capability that this predicate is meant to express.") 
