(#$comment #$grossDomesticProduct "(#$grossDomesticProduct GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$Money MONEY is a measure of the value of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's total domestic production of goods and services during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a time period -- for example, a calendar year such as (#$YearFn 1997) or a calendar quarter such as (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1997)); but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  MONEY will sometimes be specified using the function #$USDollarFn, which returns a #$UnitOfMoney denominated in US dollars of a particular year; for example, to express the fact that the gross domestic product of the United Arab Emirates for 1997 was $35,930,000,000 in 1990 U.S. dollars, we can say (#$grossDomesticProduct #$UnitedArabEmirates (#$YearFn 1997) ((#$USDollarFn 1990) 3.593e+10)).  See also #$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal and #$grossNationalProduct.") 
