(#$comment #$agentTypePosesThreat "This predicate can be used to represent when instances of #$Agent
all belonging to a particular (ideally, well-defined) type pose a
threat to some other instance of #$Agent.
(#$agentTypePosesThreat THREAT_AGT_TYPE AGT) means that
any instance (as a default) of THREAT_AGT_TYPE is disposed to and is
capable of acting in a way which threatens a vital interest of AGT.
The class of 'vital' interests in this sense includes (for instances
of #$Person) physical and financial well-being, (for instances of
#$Country) goals which fall under #$VitalNationalInterest,
(for other instances of #$Organization) the
ability to fulfill AGT's main function.  See #$agentPosesThreat,
after which this predicate is patterned.") 
