(#$comment #$SystemSlot "A collection of #$Roles.  Each instance is like an
#$ActorSlot in so far as it specifies a particular individual's #$Role
with respect to a particular #$Situation.  However, unlike an
#$ActorSlot, which relates a #$SomethingExisting to an #$Event, a
#$SystemSlot relates an #$Agent to a #$FunctionalSystem, specifying a
functional role that the #$Agent plays in the system.  Unless there
are contextual or system-specific constraints to the contrary
(cf. #$FixedFunctionalSystem), an #$Agent may play multiple roles
within the same system, and may indeed play different roles at
different times in the history of the system.  Each #$SystemSlot is
associated with a certain set of expectations (see #$expected-ToBe and
#$amenable-ToBe) about how an #$Agent who has that role will behave
while playing the role, and also with a set of expected capabilities
that the #$Agent playing the role must have or maintain during the
time it plays that role.  As a rule, these expectations may be
