(#$comment #$ExtraterritorialRegion "A collection of geopolitical entities.  Each instance of #$ExtraterritorialRegion is associated with some geographical region located within the boundaries of one country but administered by officials of a foreign country.  Most commonly, extraterritoriality is extended to the grounds of diplomatic missions, including the living quarters of ambassadors.  In some cases, it has been extended to larger areas, as to the former European concessions in Shanghai that were granted by the Treaty of Nanking.  Authorities of the surrounding country cannot enter or search within an extraterritorial region without permission from the foreign authorities who administer that region (generally, the head of the diplomatic mission).") 
