(#$comment #$SubSystemUnderTraversalFn "A function, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a #$Traversal TRAV in SYS as in (#$SubSystemUnderTraversalFn SYS TRAV), returns the smallest subsystem SUB of SYS such that TRAV is a traversal in SUB (see #$traversalInSystem) and SUB is a point-closed subsystem of SYS (see #$pointClosedSubSystems).  Note that 'smallest' here means that no link LINK between X and Y in SYS is a link in SUB if neither (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X LINK Y)) nor (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList Y LINK X)) holds.  Note also that since SUB is a point-closed subsystem of SYS, every point in SYS that is on TRAV (see #$pointOnTraversal) is a point in SUB.  Note finally that since SUB is the 'smallest' subsystem of SYS in which TRAV is a traversal, SUB must be a #$ConnectedPathSystem.") 
