(#$bugtraqDiscussionText #$Bugtraq1034 "A vulnerability exists within the Microsoft Clip Art Gallery, where a  remote user can crash the Clip   Art application or possibly execute arbitrary code.  Clip art can be downloaded from any website and incorporated into the  local gallery. A particular   file format called .CIL is used in order to transport new clip art  files to the users. The vulnerability   is that a user may open a malformed .CIL file containing a long  embedded field downloaded from a   malicious third-party website or in the form of an email attachment  regardless of its origin.") 
