(#$comment #$PreparingForSituation "The collection of #$PurposefulActions in which an agent prepares for a situation (#$Situation-Temporal). The action can be entirely mental, as in #$PlanningToDoSomething, or can involve #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvents, for example, buying food as a preparation for cooking a meal. The action may make the situation prepared for more likely to happen or it may have no causal bearing on that situation. For example, preparing for college may make it more likely that the agent will attend college. However, preparing for a power outage by buying a flashlight doesn't make it more likely that the power outage will occur. See also #$PreparingForUndesirableSituation. To relate #$PreparingForSituations to the #$Situation-Temporals that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparingForFn. To relate #$PreparingForUndesirableSituations to the #$Situation-Temporals that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparednessFn. See also #$PreventFromHappening and #$PreventionFn.") 
