(#$comment #$GridError "The most general collection of grid error events; a subset of #$Malfunction, and a subset of #$SystemCondition. An instance of #$GridError is a dynamic state of impairment.  Having a grid error is an event: it has temporal aspects, it progresses dynamically, etc., it is not just `being in some static state of error.'  Some subsets of GridError are: #$MessageLost, #$ResourceBudgetExceeded, #$OrphanedTask.  If an event on the grid produces a solution which actually worsens the problem meant to be solved, that event contains an element of #$GridError.  Each #$GridError is a state of actual, developed error or impairment, rather than the event of developing an error.  Also note that each type of error, such as MessageLost, is the set of all `cases' or `instances' of grid events which have that error.") 
