(#$comment #$onPath-Alongside "This predicate relates customary paths such as 
roads and trails to things that are alongside them,
like buildings, towns, parks, and trees.  
(#$onPath-Alongside THING PATH) means that THING is located
right beside a portion of PATH (see #$alongsidePathSegment).
THING need not be touching PATH, but must be #$near PATH.
Thus a house set very far back from the street might fail to
be alongside it, while the lot on which the house sits _is_ 
alongside the street.  There should be no other object of the 
same type as THING, nor any object as large or larger than
THING, standing between THING and PATH.  THING might be on 
both sides of PATH at once (e.g. a road going through a park), 
and might even spatially contain a portion of PATH; but PATH 
must not terminate strictly inside of THING (e.g. the path 
must begin and end at least at the park's edges, if not 
outside them).") 
