(#$comment #$nthStreetOver "This predicate relates a street to another street that 
is a specified number of \"streets over\" from the first.
(#$nthStreetOver STREET1 STREET2 N) means that STREET1 and
STREET2 run parallel to each other in some #$GridStreetSystem,
and that, for any given perpendicular street XSTREET that 
intersects both of them, the distance between the two 
intersections is a #$distanceInBlocksOfStreet of N blocks
along XSTREET.  For example, in a typical grid system, 15th
Street is five streets over from 10th Street.  Of course, 5th
Street is also five streets over from 10th Street; so to 
identify a particular street in a given context using this 
predicate, it is generally also necessary to specify a 
direction from STREET1 to STREET2.") 
