(#$comment #$directionsOfPath "This predicate can be used to state which directions a
(non-directed) spatial path such as a two-way street runs in.  
(#$directionsOfPath PATH DIR1 DIR2) means that PATH runs in a 
relatively straight line from DIR1 to DIR2 (and vice versa, of 
course).  DIR1 and DIR2 must be roughly opposite directions 
(see #$oppositeDirection-Interval).  If PATH is not relatively
straight (see #$CenterLineOfPathFn and #$Linear-Straight), or
is an instance of #$DirectedCustomaryPath, the above statement 
will be false or malformed; so #$directionsOfPath should not 
applied to such paths.") 
