(#$cyclistNotes #$PlanActionRestrictionPredicate "Planning contexts are ordinarily considered to be
'deontic', in the sense that they are descriptions of idealized
event-sequences that are supposed to occur. Thus, one way of
representing temporo-spatial constraints in plans is to simply assert
as a matter of 'fact' *that* a particular event has such-and-such
spatiotemporal characteristics.  However, this is not always
sufficient, especially in cases where the plan itself is being
critiqued against a set of background constraints. It is primarily
such background constraints that the instances of this collection are
supposed to be used to represent.") 
