(#$cyclistNotes #$AssemblyStageAttribute "This collection has an inter-arg constraint such that anything that has as an attribute an instance of #$AssemblyStageAttribute must itself be an #$Artifact.  Thus, we are committed to the claim that anything that is in the process of 'assembly' in this sense is already an #$Artifact.  Because of the definition of #$Artifact, we are also committed to the claim that anything that has an #$AssemblyStageAttribute is also at least #$PartiallyTangible.  However, there is NO commitment that the thing being assembled must already be an instance of what it will eventually be. For example, something that #$hasAttributes (#$PartlyAssembledAttributeFn #$Automobile) may or may not be an instance of #$Automobile.  Presumably, the partly assembled auto will become an #$Automobile at some stage in construction, but a commitment regarding precisely when is probably better left to the specific context.") 
