(#$cyclistNotes #$rateOfEventType-Place "One advantage to having a quaternary predicate like this (and probably                others like it) is that it allows                us to represent the frequencies or rates of various types of events                without inventing a new 'rate predicate' for each type of event.                While predicates like #$birthRate, #$crimeRate, etc. are                natural and acceptable, predicates like 'hackingAttemptRate,'                'employeeHiringRate,' 'catchingTheFluRate,' will strike                many as ad hoc.  One disadvantage, however, is that this                predicate forces us to represent the relevant event-type                in some way, whether this is by reifying a new collection                or using something like #$CollectionSubsetFn.") 
