(#$comment #$quantityChangeFunction "(#$quantityChangeFunction TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive instantaneous time slices of THING varies as instances of FUNCTION-TYPE vary.  Thus to say that 'during 1998 Fred had a net weight gain' we could say (#$quantityChangeFunction (#$YearFn 1998) Fred #$massOfObject #$NetIncreasingFunction).  This would mean that the value of #$massOfObject of Fred shows a net increase over 1998.  To say that the #$speedOfFlow is irregular throughout DribblingEvent01 one would write (#$quantityChangeFunction DribblingEvent01 DribblingEvent01 #$speedOfFlow #$IrregularFunction).  The thickness of the previously mentioned instantaneous time slices are determined by the temporal granule size of the #$Microtheory in which the statement is made.  Thus flow rate over time for a dribbling faucet would be smoother for large temporal grained contexts.  The slot in arg2 is assumed to be functional in arg3, unless e.g. #$FunctionToArg is used appropriately.  See also #$quantityInfluenceFunction for representing factors which influence but do not necessarily result in some particular kind of change in a quantity.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for other important quantity change related predicates.") 
