(#$comment #$AgentOrange "A collection.  Each instance is a portion of a #$ToxicSubstance.  #$AgentOrange is an herbicide sprayed on plants as a defoliant.  It has been used mainly in modern guerilla conflicts, notably in the #$VietnamWar.  Although #$AgentOrange is not used against troops like #$NerveGas, it is classified as a #$ChemicalWeapon because it's used to gain strategic advantage, either by reducing the amount of vegetation enemy troops can use for cover or by destroying an enemy's civilian crops.  The name is a US military code name which comes from the color of the containers used for this #$ChemicalWeapon in the #$VietnamWar.") 
