(#$comment #$operatesInRegion "(#$operatesInRegion AGT REG) relates an #$Agent AGT to a geographical region in which AGT performs (at least once) a task central to her/its job function or group mission. Positive examples of 'operating' in a region include a company buying assembly materials or selling goods in REG, a #$HumanitarianOrganization performing its mission in REG, a #$TravelingSalesPerson working in REG, etc.  Negative examples include people who visit a region strictly for hobby-related or personal reasons.  Borderline cases include a #$HumanitarianOrganization which raises money in an area but which does not perform its primary function there, and a #$TerroristGroup which takes sanctuary in REG but which does not conduct terrorist operations there.  See also #$performsInsAtLocation and rules linking the two predicates.") 
