(#$comment #$IAForensicsReport-DiscoveryOfTrojanSnifferOnForwardOpsCenterSecretCommandLAN "A report issued by #$DLAForwardJ6Officer, informing the #$JTFCommander that when the intermittent modem connection reported in   #$IAIncidentReport-DiscoveryOfIntermittentModemConnection was active, the suspect PC was connected to the Secret Command LAN and that the PC's network interface card was operating in promiscuous mode.  A software-based sniffer was subsequently  discovered in the WindowsSystem directory. The sniffer was a Trojan of the  normal systray.exe file that should be 37KB in size. The sniffer Trojan  file was 367KB in size. Sniffed data was stored in a dummy backup registry  file, sys.bak. All sites are urged to immediately check all PCs in their  enclaves for such Trojan files, NIC in promiscuous mode, and modems  on PC connected to Secret or SBU LANs.") 
