(#$comment #$Endospore "When in a hostile environment, some bacteria become
dormant in the form of an #$Endospore. #$Endospores are very difficult to
stain unless special techniques are used. They may appear as a small white
spot in a rod shaped cell. #$Endospores are resistant to heat, chemicals
and radiation. Sterilization is the only way to inactivate an #$Endospore.
They are a nongrowing heat-resistant structure which grows within the cell
of certain bacteria. Endospores may last for years.") 
