(#$comment #$increasesLikelihood-PropProp "(#$increasesLikelihood-PropProp p1 p2) means that p1's becoming true would
increase the likelihood that p2 will be true.  This is a defeasible relationship:
not all situations in which p1 becomes true are situations in which the likelihood of
p2 is increased.  Thus (#$increasesLikelihood-PropProp  (I win the lottery) (I am happy)) could be
true even if the likelihood that I am happy is not increased in the situation in which
I win the lottery and at the same time discover that I have cancer. 
#$increasesLikelihood-PropProp can be thought of as a form of subjunctive implication,
where instead of p1's subjunctively implying p2, the likelihood of p2 would be greater
if p1 were true than if p1 were not true.  It is therefore definable in terms
of the subjunctive operator #$subImplies together with the predicate #$likelihood.  
See also #$cfImplies and #$causes-PropProp.") 
