(#$comment #$adjacentPathsAtJunction "(adjacentPathsAtJunction JUNCT PATH) means that the #$JunctionOfPaths JUNCT has PATH as one of the paths (instances of #$Path-Generic) joining it.  A junction may connect many paths (it must connect at least three distinct paths), and a path may pass through many junctions, and may end at a junction.  Examples: all the streets meeting at a certain #$Intersection-Street, the particular #$Trachea and both primary bronchi meeting at the #$TracheobronchialJunction between a certain person's #$Lungs, and three #$LongitudeLines intersecting at the #$SouthPole.  Neither PATH nor JUNCTION need be instances of #$PartiallyTangible, #$TemporalThing, or #$SpatialThing; however if PATH is, JUNCTION must also be.") 
