(#$comment #$NodesCut-SubSystemFn "A function that, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a set SET of nodes in SYS (i.e., a subset of (#$NodesFn SYS)) as in (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET), gives the subsystem SUBSYS of SYS obtained by cutting all nodes in SET from SYS.  The 'cutting' of nodes also removes all their attached loops and links (and points on them if any).  More strictly, SUBSYS is determined as follows: (i) SUBSYS is a subsystem of SYS (i.e., (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds), (ii) (#$NodesFn SUBSYS) = (#$NodesFn SYS) - SET, (#$LinksFn SUBSYS) = (#$LinksFn SYS) - {LINK: LINK is a link in SYS and X is on LINK for some node X in SET}, (#$PointsFn SUBSYS) = ((#$PointsFn SYS) - SET) - {Y: Y is a non-node-point in SYS and Y is on LINK for some LINK in ((#$LinksFn SYS) - (#$LinksFn SUBSYS)), and (#$LoopsFn SUBSYS) = (#$LoopsFn SYS) - {LOOP: LOOP is a loop in SYS and X is on LOOP for some X in SET}.  Note that since there is no 'empty' #$PathSystem, SET must be a proper subset of (#$NodesFn SYS) for (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) to be defined.") 
