(#$comment #$groupMemberType "The predicate #$groupMemberType is used in characterizing the members of a particular group.  (#$groupMemberType GROUP TYPE) means that all of GROUP's members are elements of the collection TYPE.  For example, to state that the #$groupMembers of the Austin City Council are humans, one would write (#$groupMemberType AustinCityCouncil #$Person).  The members of a particular group might be characterized in more than one way; e.g., a Hispanic Business Council may have both the #$groupMemberType #$EthnicGroupOfHispanics and the #$groupMemberType #$BusinessPerson (provided that all of its members are Hispanic business people).  For 'typical' or 'expected' characteristics of members, see also #$memberTypes and #$typeHasTypicalMemberTypes.") 
