(#$comment #$WorldWideWebHomePage "#$WorldWideWebHomePage is a subset of #$WorldWideWebPage. Every instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage is the 'entrance' into a #$WorldWideWebSite. Visitors typically go to this page first, and navigate via hyperlinks from there to other pages in the site. The homepage usually has a simple URL of the form http://www.NAME.SUFFIX, where NAME is the one-word name of the site and SUFFIX is a suffix indicating the nature or geographical location of the site. Common suffixes include 'com' (commercial), 'edu' (educational), 'gov' (government), and 'org' (non-profit organization). original comment by Kathy Burns") 
