(#$comment #$relationInstanceAll "(#$relationInstanceAll PRED INS1 COL2) means that, for every instance of COL2 (INS2) there is a relation PRED with INS1, i.e. (PRED INS1 INS2) holds. For example, to state that 'each State in the Union is a subdivision of the United States', one would assert: (#$relationInstanceAll    #$geopoliticalSubdivision #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$State-UnitedStates) in place of a rule that would say the same thing. #$relationInstanceAll is thus redundant with a huge set of commonly-occurring rules. One must be aware of the implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ") 
