(#$comment #$actionExpressesFeelingToward "(#$actionExpressesFeelingToward ACTION FEELING OBJECT) means that the
doer (#$doneBy) of ACTION expresses FEELING about OBJECT by doing
ACTION.  Example uses include 'protesters burned a flag to express their hatred of the government', or 'Joe donned a Zoot suit to express his nostalgia for the 1920's.'  See also
#$actionExpressesFeeling, #$feelsTowardsObject, #$feelsTowardsEvent.  Note that this predicate describes feelings expressed about OBJECT and does not necessarily entail communicating feelings to OBJECT.  To represent the communication of emotions to others see #$CommunicationAct-Single, #$NonVerbalCommunicating.") 
