(#$comment #$authorityCapableOf "The predicate #$authorityCapableOf is used to assert that a
particular agent has the authority to participate in a certain kind of
situation in the capacity of a particular role, because of said
agent's intrinsic properties.  (#$authorityCapableOf AGENT SITTYPE
ROLE) means that AGENT is authorized by the appropriate agency of
authorization to play the role ROLE in situations of type SITTYPE. For
example, it is true in Orange County that (#$authorityCapableOf
LanceIto #$Trial-Criminal #$judicialAgents). Note that even though an
agent may be #$authorityCapableOf playing a certain role in a certain
kind of situation, this does not necessarily imply that the agent will
be physically or mentally capable of playing that role in every
instance of the situation type, or even that the agent is physically
or mentally capable in general of playing that role in situations of
that type.") 
