(#$bugtraqDiscussionText #$Bugtraq663 "A buffer overflow vulnerabilityin GNOME's shared libraries handling  of the 'espeaker' command   line argument may allow local users to attack setuid binaries linked  against these libraries to obtain   root access.  Calling a program linked against GNOME with the command like  arguments '--enable-sound   --espeaker=<80 byte buffer>' results in a buffer overflow.   One known setuid root program linked against these libraries in the  Mandrake 6.0 distribution is   '/usr/games/nethack'.  It is likely this is a vulnerability in the libesd shared library  instead of libgnome. In that case esound   0.2.8 would be vulnerable.") 
