(#$comment #$preservesRelnBetweenArgs "(#$preservesRelnBetweenArgs FN BIN-PRED N) means that if
NAT1 and NAT2 are non-atomic terms generated by means of FN, and
(BINPRED ARG1 ARG2) is known to be true, and ARG1 appears as the Nth
argument of NAT1 and ARG2 appears as then Nth argument of NAT2, then
(BIN-PRED NAT1 NAT2).") 
(#$comment #$transferRouter-Generic "This predicate can be used to indicate whatever acts as a router in an instance of           #$GeneralizedTransfer and therefore plays an active and crucial role in it.            (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS THING) means that THING acts as a router            in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANS.  For example, suppose a trip TRANS via             airplane taking a person PER from New York to Austin makes a stop in #$CityOfOmahaNB,            where PER changes flights.  If 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport-Org' is the instance of             #$AirportOrganization running the airport located in the #$CityOfOmahaNB, then            we can (probably) say that 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport-Org' is a router in the #$GeneralizedTransfer            TRANS of PER and represent            this by (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport-Org').  See also            #$transferRelay-Generic.") 
(#$comment #$toPossessor "This predicate identifies an #$Agent who gains some right to use an object.  (#$toPossessor GAIN AGENT) means that after the event GAIN (a #$GainingUserRights), AGENT enjoys some #$UserRightsAttribute over the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer which that agent did not have at the start of GAIN.") 
