(#$comment #$UnaryActionPredicate "The collection of one-place action predicates (please see
the comment on #$ActionPredicate) used to make assertions about what
an agent does in some special context. Instances of
#$UnaryActionPredicate are similar to intransitive verbs. An example
might be the English sentence 'Bob stands up', which could be turned
into a CycL action assertion by way of a predicate 'standsUp'. The
CycL assertion '(standsUp Bob)' (asserted in a specially created
microtheory) would result in the generation of an assertion of
something like the following:
(and 
(isa StandingUp01 MovementProcess) 
(performedBy StandingUp01 Bob)
(holdsIn (StartFn StandingUp01) (postureOfAnimal Bob RecliningPosture))
(holdsIn (EndFn StandingUp01) (postureOfAnimal Bob UprightPosture)))") 
