(#$comment #$objectMoving "The predicate #$objectMoving is used to refer to an object which is moving in a particular #$MovementEvent. (#$objectMoving MOVE OBJECT) means that OBJECT is in motion at some point during the #$MovementEvent MOVE and is either the #$primaryObjectMoving in MOVE or #$subEvents of MOVE.  OBJECT need not move from the #$fromLocation to the #$toLocation.  If it does, and moves along the trajectory of MOVE, then it is a #$primaryObjectMoving, part of a #$primaryObjectMoving, or contained in a #$primaryObjectMoving.  A part of or object contained by a #$primaryObjectMoving may or may not also be #$primaryObjectMoving.") 
