(#$comment #$symptomOfAilment "If (#$symptomOfAilment SYMPTOM AILMENT), then instances of AILMENT are often associated with instances of SYMPTOM and if someone has the ailment and the symptom it is likely that the ailment causes the symptom.  If one is attempting to diagnose an illness the presence of a symptom of an ailment increases the likelihood that one suffers from the ailment.  For instance, (#$symptomOfAilment #$FluLikeSymptoms #$Influenza), 
so, all else being equal, the chances of one having the flu
if one has flulike symptoms are greater than the chances of having the flu if 
one does not have these symptoms.") 
