(#$comment #$onResume-CoABS "(onResume-CoABS ?MESSAGE ?RESUME) means that ?MESSAGE is a message which  is on the #$Resume-CoABS of an #$Agent-CoABS. Minimally, this includes a  #$GridAddress-CoABS. The rest of the fields are optional. These will include a  list of capacities, of #$Languages the agent can decipher, and a history. This last, includes what #$Communities-CoABS the agent joined, the success rate, and possibly reasons for failure, particularly when said reasons are outside the  control of the agent. In the CoABSMt all agents have a resume.  In their case, it might not wholly be filled in by that #$Agent, but other  agents may add to it! For example, an #$Agent-CoABS with the #$Capacity  #$AgentCapacity-AddToResume or #$AgentCapacity-Police can add to an agent's resume.") 
