(#$comment #$distanceInBlocksOfStreet "This predicate relates two things located in a 
city or town in terms of the number of blocks away they 
are from each other.  (#$distanceInBlocksOfStreet OBJ1 OBJ2 N)
means that in order to get from OBJ1 to OBJ2 by the shortest
route using city streets, one must travel a total of N 
instances of #$BlockOfStreet.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 must each be
#$onPath some instance or other of #$Street-Generic, and if
they are on different streets, those streets must be (directly
or indirectly) connected to each other within the same 
#$StreetSystem.  Since the lengths of street blocks vary 
considerably, a given distance in street blocks cannot be 
generally associated with any specific absolute distance.  
Still, this predicate is useful for rough estimates of, and 
comparisons between, distances.") 
