(#$statementOfPurpose #$AmnestyInternational "`Amnesty International has a precise mandate, detailed in an international statute. The main focus of its campaigning is to: free all prisoners of conscience (...people detained anywhere for their beliefs or because of their ethnic origin, sex, colour, language, national or social origin, economic status, birth or other status, who have not used or advocated violence), ensure fair and prompt trials for political prisoners, abolish the death penalty, torture and other cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment of prisoners, [and] end extrajudicial executions and `disappearances'.  Amnesty International also opposes abuses by opposition groups, including hostage taking, torture and killings of prisoners and other deliberate and arbitrary killings.'") 
