(#$comment #$physicalPortions "(#$physicalPortions WHOLE PART) means PART is a representative spatial chunk of WHOLE.  Every intrinsic property which is true of WHOLE should be true of PART.  Spatial parts of WHOLE which are not representative of the whole would be #$physicalParts or #$physicalDecompositions, not #$physicalPortions.  For example, the SpaghettiSauce001 which is part of SpaghettiDinner001 is a #$physicalParts of the dinner.  A #$physicalPortions of the dinner would include some sauce, some noodles, some parmesan cheese, etc. - parts of all the #$constituents.   This is the spatial analog of #$timeSlices (not #$subEvents). (#$Pittman, 6/25/96)") 
