(#$comment #$conceptuallyRelated "The purpose of this predicate is to record the existence of a conceptual link between two Cyc constants that would otherwise require a very complex explicit assertion to be related to one another. Good examples of such couples are #$PublicTransportationDevice and #$PublicTransportationScheduleDocument or #$Dog and #$DogFood. The knowledge representation philosophy here is similar to that behind many #$RuleMacroPredicates. Having complex relationships represented -- possibly redundantly -- in a more compact fashion makes for faster retrieval. Because Cyc constants can be conceptually related in many different ways, no explicit definition for this predicate is provided.") 
