(#$comment #$trueFormula "(#$trueFormula P) denotes that P is true.
#$trueFormula is used to encapsulate a formula so that the formula
may receive special handling during canonicalization and inference. 
Specifically, a variable (e.g., ?formula) appearing as an argument 
to a logical operator will be canonicalized as (#$trueFormula ?formula),
and a universally quantified formula appearing within a disjunction 
(e.g., (#$implies (#$forAll ?x P(?x)) Q)) will be canonicalized as a 
trueFormula (e.g., (#$implies (#$trueFormula (#$forAll ?x P(?x))) Q)). 
During inference a closed #$trueFormula literal will be deemed satisfied 
when it can be proved from the assertions in accessible mts (i.e., it 
will be treated as an intensional ask).") 
