(#$comment #$permissionMode "(#$permissionMode FILE MODE) means that FILE has a set of  file permissions represented by MODE, where MODE is a four-digit octal  number.  The number corresponds to a particular configuration of  permission settings.  The leftmost digit indicates whether or not the  file is SUID (4) or SGID (2).  From left to right, the remaining  digits indicate   the priviledges had by the file's owner, the files owner's group, and   others. In each case, 1 represents execute priviledge, 2 indicates  write priviledge, and 4 indicates read priviledge.  So, for example,  (#$permissionMode File001 0655) means that File001's owner can read and  write FileOO1 (but not execute it), and everyone else can read and  execute it.") 
