(#$comment #$commutativeInArgsAndRest "(commutativeInArgsAndRest REL ARGNUM-1 ARGNUM-2 ... ARGNUM-N)
means that REL is commutative with respect to each of the
argument positions ARGNUM-1, ARGNUM-2, ..., and ARGNUM-N, and all argument positions greater than N.  For example, (#$commutativeInArgsAndRest REL 2) means that all arguments to REL but the first are commutative.  So 
(REL A B C) would be equivalent to (REL A C B), but A could not commute.
(#$commutativeInArgs REL 2 3 5) means that the second, third, fifth, and
greater argument positions of REL are commutative, but not necessarily the first or fourth.  (Since REL is an instance of #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation, it 
must have at least two argument positions that are commutative, and at least
one that is _not_ commutative.)") 
