(#$comment #$BroadcastContract-CoABS "A #$BroadcastContract-CoABS accompanies a #$Broadcast-CoABS sent out by an #$Agent-CoABS with #$AgentCapacity-CoABS: User. The idea is that the user  can place constraints on answering the query asked. For example, they might state  a maximum of money they are willing to spend on having a question answered.  Also, they might need the information by a certain time and date. The other  sort of information a user can include are stipulations about secrecy or security measures, a suggestion as to which #$AgentCapacity-CoABS will be minimally needed to answer the question/query. Only two fields on the contract are  mandatory: the broadcast name (so that agents know which contract attends which  broadcast), and the user's #$GridAddress-CoABS. All the other fields on the broadcast contract are optional: negotiation can take place post hoc.") 
