(#$comment #$TestHypotheticalConstant1 "#$TestHypotheticalConstant1 is used for certain elements of #$TestQuestionMicrotheory.  For example one of the ways this would be necessary is for hypothetical asks that bind expressions involving #$TheSetOf in there answers.  When this happens, it becomes possible to reference a term created in the hypothetical microtheory in the microtheoty of the question.  For questions which reference hypothesized constants in their answers, it would be impossible to specify a target binding list, since a new hypothesized constant is created afresh in every new image in which the Ask is run.  The thing to do in these cases is use a constant such as #$TestHypotheticalConstant1 in the #$testAnswersCycL.  The testing code will match wherever #$TestHypotheticalConstant1 occurs in #$testAnswersCycL with any constants whose name begins with 'HYP-' which appear in the binding list returned by the ask being tested.. If your #$testAnswersCycL references more than one distinct hypothesized constant, then use #$TestHypotheticalConstant2, 3, etc.. You may need to reify a new constant if necessary.") 
