(#$comment #$assistsInActionByDoing "(#$assistsInActionByDoing AGENT ACTION01 ACTION02) means that AGENT is one of the agents assisting in the performance of ACTION01, and that AGENT's assistance consists in doing ACTION02. AGENT itself may or may not also be one of the performers of ACTION01. ACTION02 must not be a sub-event of ACTION01. In general, (#$thereExists ?HELP (#$assistsInActionByDoing AGENT ACTION01 ?HELP))) is equivalent to (#$assistingAgent ACTION01 AGENT). For example, if the US carries out a bombing campaign (ACTION01) against Iraq using Saudi air bases, with help from Saudi ground crews (ACTION02) but no direct Saudi involvement in the attack, then (#$assistsInActionByDoing #$SaudiArabia ACTION01 ACTION02), and also (#$assistingAgent #$SaudiArabia ACTION01). See the comment on #$assistingAgent for further examples of the use of that predicate.") 
