(#$comment #$supplyAmountDuring "(#$supplyAmountDuring PT COL THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT is supplied during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyAmountDuring is very general.  PT might, for example, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and the range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT during the temporal extent of THING.") 
