(#$cyclistNotes #$Y2KIndividualFn "It might be preferrable to merge #$Y2KIndividualFn onto #$Y2KFn instead of having two constants that differ only in their argument constraints. This should NOT be done without testing to ensure that it functions as well or better than the two functions as currently defined. For example, if the arg1 of #$Y2KFn is weakened to #$Thing, then #$Y2KFn could take instances of #$Individual and #$Collection. However, one would need to unassert the #$resultGenlArg and #$intersectionType assertions on #$Y2KFn because they require that arg1 take instances of #$Collection. These assertions are important to the desired performance of #$Y2KFn. To preserve the functionality these assertions provide, one could add two rules patterned after the #$expansionAxioms of these two #$RuleMacroPredicates, with an additional clause in the antecedent, so that the rule fires only when (#$arg1Isa #$Y2KFn Collection). Since #$Y2KFn is working so well, resulting in many dependent assertions, MichaelW decided to go the conservative route and create two constants.") 
