(#$comment #$ElectronicAttack-DestructionOfInformation "#$ElectronicAttack-DestructionOfInformation is a subset of #$ElectronicAttack-CorruptionOfInformation and an instance of #$ElectronicAttackTypeByPurpose. It is the collection of 
electtonic attacks that involve the destruction of information on their victim's #$ComputationalSystems. Like #$ElectronicAttack-Vandalism,
#$ElectronicAttack-DestructionOfInformation requires a deliberate,
malicious intention to corrupt information possessed by the victim.  
Unlike vandalism, all instances of destruction of information must
have as their primary purpose the willful destruction of that
information.  A website defacement where someone posted critical
information or unwanted images would not qualify, whereas an
attack where the primary purpose was the deleting of files would qualify.") 
