(#$comment #$outranksOnScale "(#$outranksOnScale PERSON1 PERSON2 SCALE) means that the subabstraction of PERSON1 that is referenced in the context of the assertion outranks the subabstraction of PERSON2 that is referenced in the context, on same military rank scale SCALE.  This generally means that for the duration of the time interval in which the assertion is asserted to hold (via #$holdsIn, or a temporally qualified Mt) PERSON1 is authorized to issue certain sorts of orders to PERSON2, which PERSON2 is in turn required to obey.  Since an outranksOnScale assertion will almost never hold true generally of a pair of entities, it should be qualified via #$holdsIn or deliberately reified subabstractions, or else be asserted within a temporally constrained context.") 
