(#$comment #$mtOfCulture "This predicate relates microtheories to the cultures 
  they are relevant for or pertain to.  (#$mtOfCulture MT CULTURE) 
  means that the assertions in MT are made, and considered true, 
  from the perspective of CULTURE.  Beyond this, the precise type of 
  relevance or pertinence will depend on other dimension attributes 
  for MT, including modality.  For a more specialized predicate 
  that relates a culture to the microtheory that precisely 
  specifies its associated beliefs, practices, and artifacts, see 
  #$mtDefinesCulture.  See also #$mtCultureBeliefs.") 
