(#$comment #$DiplomaticSupport "#$DiplomaticSupport is a collection of attributes representing the different generic levels of diplomatic support that one country can give to another. Attributes in this collection represent the general commitment of one diplomatic agent (e.g., a country or organization of   countries) to provide diplomatic support to another agent, as evidenced by pledges and/or present or previous behavior. For example, (#$givesSupportToAgent #$GreatBritain-TheIsland #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$HighAmountFn #$DiplomaticSupport)). Note that such relationships are liable to change and, therefore, assertions about them should have a temporal qualification (see #$holdsIn).  Diplomatic support is intangible but significant, in that it may affect actions in international organizations, it may influence third parties,   and it may imply or include economic or military support. (See also #$MilitarySupport and #$EconomicSupport.)  To represent actual events in which support is given, see #$ShowingSupportForSomeone and #$HelpingAnAgent.--Lupher, June 23, 1998") 
