(#$comment #$instantiatesToRuleMacro "Suppose PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate that is type-level in at least one argument position, and that INST-PRED is an 'instance-level analog' of PRED that is instance-level in at least one argument position in which PRED is type-level.  (#$instantiatesToRuleMacro MACRO PRED INST-PRED) means that if (PRED ARG1COL ARG2COL) is known to be true, (MACRO INST-PRED ARG1COL ARG2COL) is known to be true.  For example, suppose we decide that in a certain reasoning context (#$colorOfType COL COLOR) means that, for every instance INST of COL, (#$colorOfObject INST COLOR), i.e., that (#$relationAllInstance #$colorOfObject COL COLOR).  We would express this by asserting (#$instantiatesToRuleMacro #$relationAllInstance #$colorOfType #$colorOfObject).") 
