(#$comment #$changesQuantityByAmount "This predicate specifies the amount by which a given quantity changes in a given time period.  (#$changesQuantityByAmount TIME THING SLOT AMOUNT) means that during TIME, THING's #$QuantitySlot SLOT changes by AMOUNT.  TIME is a #$TemporalThing, and AMOUNT is a #$ScalarInterval (which may be positive, negative, or #$None).  For instance, (#$changesQuantityByAmount (#$YearFn 1980) #$SaudiArabia #$oilExport (#$MillionBarrelsPerYear 1)) means that in 1980, Saudi Arabia's oil export increased by 1 million barrels per day.  See also: #$changesQuantityByFraction, #$changesQuantityInDirection.") 
