(#$comment #$differentSymbols "A variable-arity predicate used to state the non-identity of symbols.  (#$differentSymbols X1 X2 ... Xn) is true whenever each of the X's is a symbol which is different from all the others. Note that
two symbols can pick out the same individual or class of individuals and
still be different symbols; e.g., 'Bertrand Russell' and 'the author of
'On Denoting'' both pick out the same individual, but are different symbols.
Two symbols can even be identical in meaning and yet still be different
symbols; e.g., 'bachelor' and 'unmarried male.'

For the stronger case, where each of the X's picks out something which is not 
identical with what is picked out by any of the other X's, see #$different.") 
