(#$comment #$infoPathway-Partial "The predicate #$infoPathway-Partial is used to indicate that the instance of          #$InformationBearingThing transferred for some instance of #$InformationTransferEvent follows some section of an          instance of #$Path-Spatial during some portion of the transfer.           (#$infoPathway-Partial TRANS PATH) means that part of the route of TRANS           is spatial and follows PATH.  For example, consider an e-mail SUCCESSFULY sent
          from one PC to another (i.e. the information CONTENT of the instance of #$InformationBearingThing
          transferred is SUCCESSFULLY transferred).  Suppose this transfer of information INFOTRANS occurs along several
          distinct cables.  If one of these cables is CABLE001,
          then we may correctly assert (#$infoPathway-Partial INFOTRANS CABLE001).  See also
          #$infoPathway-Complete.  Note that in the example above, it would be incorrect
          to replace #$infoPathway-Partial with #$infoPathway-Complete, since the entire
          transfer did not occur along CABLE001.") 
