(#$comment #$attempts "(#$attempts AGENT ACT) means that AGENT attempts to perform action
ACT. Attempts are generally regarded as initial segments of actions: think
of Joe's attempt to buy flowers as the early portion of what would be, if
completed, a flowers-buying action. Also, attempts are intrinsically
intentional: the initial portion of an action constitutes an attempt only
if it occurs because of the agent's intention to perform the action.") 
