(#$comment #$SolidStateOfMatter "One of the basic physical states of matter.  #$SolidStateOfMatter characterizes pieces of matter which are at a sufficiently low enough temperature or high enough pressure for the particular type of matter involved that the molecules of the matter are bonded to each other by various sorts of forces, and don't move away from their neighbors.  Solid objects are characterized at the macroscopic level by definite, persistent boundaries, independent of container.  Examples of things that typically have this #$AttributeValue are: a piece of aluminum foil, a lump of coal, a quartz crystal, a gold ingot stored in Fort Knox.") 
