(#$comment #$increasesCausallyOverPeriod "(#$increasesCausallyOverPeriod EVENT THING SLOT PERIOD) means that
EVENT causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING to be
greater immediately after (#$STIF q.v.)  PERIOD than it was
immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) PERIOD.  PERIOD must start no earlier
than EVENT starts in order to prevent effects preceeding their causes.
If PERIOD ends before EVENT, it still must be the case that the value
of SLOT applied to THING must be greater immediately following EVENT
than it was immediately before EVENT.  Like with
#$increasesImmediately, the increase need not be monotonic.  This
predicate is agnostic as to whether the increase occurs during EVENT
or after it.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of
related predicates.") 
