(#$comment #$relationInstanceExistsMax "(#$relationInstanceExistsMax PRED INS1 COL2 N) means that there exist
at most N instances (INS2) of COL2 that have the relation PRED with
INS1, i.e. (PRED INS1 INS2) holds. It allows assertions that
correspond more directly to common database entries, e.g. 'Iran has at
most three oil fields' is represented by a single GAF,
(#$relationInstanceExistsMax #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
#$OilField 3), rather than by a rule:  (#$thereExistAtMost 3 ?OILFIELD
(#$and (#$isa ?OILFIELD #$OilField) (#$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran
?OILFIELD))).  #$relationInstanceExistsMax is thus redundant with a
huge set of commonly-occurring rules.  One must be aware of the
implicit quantification underlying this predicate. ") 
