(#$comment #$Destroy-MilitaryTask "To destroy is to physically render an enemy  force combat-ineffective until it is reconstituted. Alternatively, to destroy a combat system is to damage it so badly that it cannot perform any function or be restored to a usable condition without being entirely rebuilt. The amount of damage needed to render a unit combat-ineffective depends on the unit's type, discipline, and morale. It normally requires greater than percent personnel or equipment casualties. Destroying armored or dug-in targets with area fire weapons requires a large amount of ammunition and  considerable time, so forces do not normally attempt it unless they have terminally guided munitions.") 
