predicates, with the exception of #$enables-ImpartsSkills. Motivation:
occasionally one needs to label a broad class of events as generically
`enabling', i.e., as events that enable an agent to do something in one or
the other sense of enabling. This predicate should be used sparingly: When
describing the enabling relation between a specific event or type of event,
an agent and a specific action or type of action, one should use the
specific enablesXXX predicate appropriate to that circumstance.") 
