(#$comment #$hyphenSemTrans "(hyphenSemTrans ?STRINGS ?WORD ?PART ?TRANS) means, just as with #$multiWordSemTrans, that the translation of the phrase or word containing STRINGS and WORD, with part of speech PART, is TERM. (See #$multiWordSemTrans and #$hyphenString for further usage notes). In addition, this predicate specifies that STRINGS and WORD may occur in THREE juxtapositions: they may be separated not only 1: by a space, but also 2: with a hyphen or 3: run together with no space at all. For example, (#$hyphenSemTrans (\"brown\") #$Haired-TheWord #$Adjective (#$hairColor :NOUN #$Scalp #$Brown-HairColor)) means that `brownhaired', `brown-haired', and `brown haired' all have the translation in the last argument.") 
