(#$bugtraqDiscussionText #$Bugtraq870 " A vulnerability in the Linux kernel's TCP/IP allows local users to crash, hang or corrupt the system.   A local user can crash, hang or currupt the system by sending out a  packet with options longer   than the maximum IP packet length. An easy way to generate such  packet is by using the command   'ping -s 65468 -R ANYADDRESS'. The -R option is for the IP record  route option. Under   kernel versions 2.2.X the command will fail with an message of  'message too long'.   The vulnerability seems to be the result of the kenel not checking  aif packet with options is longer                       than the maximum packet size. A long packet seems to lead to memory  corruption.") 
