(#$comment #$SemiSolidTangibleThing "A collection of tangible
things which are tactually intermediate between solids and fluids.
When a force is first applied to a semisolid object, it deforms
substantially and does not break or crack. It may return to its
original shape, like a sponge, or retain the shape which resulted from
the application of force, like soft clay. Like #$SolidTangibleThings,
semisolids have shapes independent of their containers (they satisfy
(hasAttributes ?X #$ContainerIndependentShape)) and they cannot be 
poured.") 
