(#$comment #$enables-ImpartsSkills "This predicate expresses the notion of 'enabling' in the sense of
furnishing to someone the skills she needs for the performance of a certain
type of action. This is the sense in which training or education may be
enabling factors in a person's life. Therefore, (#$enables-ImpartsSkills CIRC
SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that, in circumstance CIRC, SIT causes AGENT to
have skills sufficient for the successful performance of tokens of
ACT_TYPE, assuming that CIRC is favorable. In essence, SIT causes AGENT to
be #$skillCapableOf ACT_TYPE: SIT cause AGENT to be in a certain state, the
state we can label as 'having skills sufficient for ACT_TYPE'. The
assumption that CIRC is favorable is necessary because even a skilled agent
would not be expected to perform successfully if the general circumstances
were unfavorable.") 
