(#$comment #$cooperatingParticipants "This predicate can be used to indicate that a particular agent
participates in a particular cooperation event in order to further the
goals of that event.  (#$cooperatingParticipants COOP AGENT) means that
AGENT participates in COOP in such a way as to further the goal(s) of  
COOP, and does so at least in part for that very reason.  (Note that
AGENT might also have other reasons for participating in COOP.)  AGENT
is both a #$socialParticipants and a #$deliberateActors in COOP, and
there is at least one other AGENT2 such that 
(#$partnersInCooperation AGENT AGENT2 COOP) holds.  Example-positive:
the #$UnitedStatesArmy cooperating with the Red Cross in an instance of
#$ReliefOperation.  (But note that the individual soldiers involved in
the operation might not be #$cooperatingParticipants.)  
Example-negative: a construction worker helping to build a post office,
not so that there will be a post office in that area, but in order to earn 
money to feed her family.") 
