(#$comment #$EmptinessOfAbnormalityNote "Why are there
so few assertions under #$exceptWhen, #$exceptFor, and
#$abnormal ? The reason for this is that assertions
entered using #$exceptWhen and #$exceptFor canonicalize
into statements using #$abnormal, and so after assertion
they do not appear under these constants.  And because
of the way indexing is currently handled, most statements
using #$abnormal are not indexed under #$abnormal. They
appear as meta-assertions on the rules that they modify.
TOK 9/97") 
