(#$comment #$purposeOfEvent "When (#$purposeOfEvent EVENT GOAL) is asserted within the context of a
          particular planning context, this means that the purpose of EVENT within the
          planning context is GOAL. What this implies will vary from context to context:
          however there will often be the entailment that rational agents in the context who are
          tasked with performing the EVENT in question will themselves have GOAL as a
          goals. For the present, we remain agnostic as to how an event may inherit a
          'purpose', apart from stipulating that (#$purposeInEvent AGENT EVENT GOAL)
          implies (#$purposeOfEvent EVENT GOAL). However, it seems fairly certain that
          (#$purposeOfEvent EVENT GOAL) implies that there is an Agent performing EVENT
          who has GOAL as a purpose: for this reason the first argument is constrained to be a
          #$GenericPurposefulAction.  Also, see  purposeOfEvent-GoalType.") 
