(#$comment #$transitiveViaArgInverse "(#$transitiveViaArgInverse PRED1 PRED2 INT) means that the INTth argument position of PRED1 is transitive with respect to the _inverse_ of PRED2.  This means if we have an axiom of the form (PRED1 . ARGS), it would be correct to also have another axiom of the form (PRED1 . ARGS-PRIME), where ARGS-PRIME is the same as ARGS except the INTth arg, X, is replaced by another term Y such that (PRED2 Y X).  For example, given (#$relationAllExists #$anatomicalParts #$Mammal #$Head-AnimalBodyPart) and  (#$transitiveViaArgInverse #$relationAllExists #$genls 2), the axiom (#$relationAllExists #$anatomicalParts #$Cat #$Head-AnimalBodyPart) would be true.  See also #$transitiveViaArg.") 
