(#$comment #$agentThreatensInterest "(#$agentThreatensInterest THREAT-AGT AGT INTEREST) means that (i) AGT has INTEREST as an interest -- i.e. (#$goals AGT INTEREST) or (#$positiveVestedInterest AGT INTEREST) -- and (ii) THREAT-AGT is disposed to act in a way which would endanger INTEREST.  THREAT-AGT must be aware that her actions might damage INTEREST, and must be capable of acting as she intends.  The notion of 'posing a threat' here is as follows.  If INTEREST is a #$CycFormula, then THREAT-AGT intends to act in a way which would significantly lessen the chances of INTEREST being true.  If INTEREST is a #$TemporalThing, AGT intends to act in a way which would 'damage' INTEREST in some way -- its health, its ability to function properly, its profitability, etc.") 
