(#$comment #$eventOccursNear "The predicate #$eventOccursNear is used to give an approximate location for an event.  (#$eventOccursNear EVENT LOC) means that EVENT occurs at a place near (see #$near-Generic) LOC.  #$eventOccursNear is useful when the more exact #$eventOccursAt is unknown, hard to specify, or not worth reifying.  For example, #$eventOccursNear is useful for describing the location of events in scenarios such as `Bob was cycling by the dam', `We played checkers near the TV', and `He is standing by the horse's hind legs'.  See #$cyclistNotes for ideas on how to formalize this.") 
