(#$comment #$minimize "#$minimize allows Cyc to assume that a statement is not
true unless it is known to be true.  Specifically, if for some
bindings of the variables that appear in the minimized formula the
formula with the bindings substituted in cannot be proved, then assume
the negation of the formula with the bindings substituted in.  From an
example in the KB: (#$minimize (#$disjointWith ?Collection
?Collection)) and binding ?Collection to #$Poodle means if we cannot
prove (#$disjointWith #$Poodle #$Poodle) assume (#$not (#$disjointWith
#$Poodle #$Poodle, i.e. assume every #$Collection is nonempty unless
we know otherwise.  In the case where we bind ?Collection to some
other variable ?Y and substituting in means if we cannot show
(#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y) then assume the negation, (#$not (#$forAll ?Y
(#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y))) which is equivalent to (#$thereExists ?Y
(#$not (#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y))). This is one of the predicates that
has been created to allow Cyc to do negation by failure.  Other
related predicates are #$minimizeExtent and #$minimizeExtentForArg. ") 
