(#$comment #$completeExtentKnown "(#$completeExtentKnown PREDICATE)  means that if we can't prove some literal (PREDICATE . args) by looking in the KB, this is an argument for its negation.  This is stronger than #$minimizeExtent, because it does not require that we do any inference to prove  (PREDICATE . args), and because it results in a stronger argument against  (PREDICATE . args).  #$completeExtentKnown is most likely to be used within a particular microtheory to say that that Mt (and all its spec-mts) know the complete extent for a predicate.  See also #$completeExtentKnownForArg.") 
