(#$bugtraqDiscussionText #$Bugtraq923 "When a new document is loaded into an IE window, IE will not update  the Security Zone settings   for that window until the new document is completely loaded. This  means that if a local document   is loaded, and then a large remote document is loaded that has  JavaScript at the very beginning,   the JavaScript may load and execute before the Security Zone settings  are updated. This could   lead to remote and untrusted JavaScript running as local trusted  code, with full access to local   files, cookies, etc.") 
