(#$comment #$changesQuantityInDirection "This predicate specifies the direction in which a given quantity changes in a given time period.  (#$changesQuantityInDirection TIME THING SLOT DIRECTION) means that during TIME, THING's #$QuantitySlot SLOT changes in DIRECTION.  TIME is a #$TemporalThing, and AMOUNT is a #$QuantityChangeAttribute.  If DIRECTION is #$Positive, this denotes an increase (#$changesQuantityInDirection (#$YearFn 1980) #$SaudiArabia #$oilExport #$Positive) means that in 1980, Saudi Arabia's oil export increased.  For predicates specifying amounts of change, see: #$changesQuantityByFraction, #$changesQuantityByAmount.  See also #$quantityChangeFunction to describe qualitative aspects of a quantity change, e.g. a spike, net decreasing, curvilinear, or slow change.") 
