(#$comment #$Pourable "A physical attribute.  #$Pourable is the structural attribute of a tangible thing that is capable of flowing.  #$Pourable things don't have intrinsic shape, but instead take the shape of their containers.  When acted on by a force, a #$Pourable thing changes shape at a rate proportional to the force.  (In addition, #$Pourable things may be easily separated into multiple pieces; however, such a separation is not a breaking or shearing.)  Mobs of particles, such as portions of sand or snow, are #$Pourable; but a gelatin-like semisolid is not.  See also #$SemiSolidTangibleThing.") 
