(#$cyclistNotes #$ComplexMilitaryTask "For the moment, we will be conservative and assume that while the existance of many #$subTasks-Military in relation to a #$MilitaryTask is a consequence of a task's being a #$ComplexMilitaryTask, it is not a sufficient condition:  i.e., 'special coordination efforts' entails more than just decomposition into subtasks.  However, we may eventually want to reverse ourselves on this, possibly even going so far as to assert a forward rule to the effect that if subTasks-Military are present, then the task is a #$ComplexMilitaryTask.  We may also want to check for the presence of subtasks as a precondition for certain kinds of #$ComplexMilitaryTask.  BR 11/98.") 
