(#$comment (#$implies (#$and (#$isa ?HYP_CONT #$HypotheticalContext) (#$isa ?PROOF_CONT #$HypotheticalContext) (#$ist ?HYP_CONT ?ANT_PROP) (#$ist ?PROOF_CONT ?CONS_PROP) (#$genlMt ?HYP_CONT ?TEMP_MT) (#$genlMt ?PROOF_CONT ?HYP_CONT) (#$termDependsOn ?HYP_CONT ?TEMP_MT) (#$termDependsOn ?PROOF_CONT ?HYP_CONT)) (#$holdsIn ?TEMP (#$implies ?ANT_PROP ?CONS_PROP))) "This rule supports temporally qualified inferences for the PQ219 complex, where it is anticipated that most of the Asks will have conditional form.  It is also anticipated that the temporally qualified query will in most cases be preceded by a conditional priming query in the appropriate temporally qualified mt.  This conditional query will set up just such a situation as is referenced in the antecedent of this rule, with a hypothetical context and proof context hanging from the temporally qualified mt, with the antecedent cached in the hypothetical context and the consequent cached in the proof context.  Thus, the hope is that once the priming conditional is Asked, we can reconstruct it within a #$holdsIn wrapper for the actual query.") 
