evaluation of an action with respect to a given outcome should be `no better than' the 
evaluation of any of its subactions with respect to that same outcome. This sounds like a reasonable 
constraint on evaluation. Think of it this way:
holding the outcome fixed, each subaction should take no more than the effort 
required for the main action of which it is part.") 
